    #500 pass 15 + pcc2widthkills: the closure that opened six registers is closed, and twelve width kills become a direction split
    
    TWO ROUNDS IN ONE COMMIT, because regress/gate_arm.sh carries both the
    51-row rewire and the new pcc2 block and cannot be split by path.  Two
    CHANGELOG blocks; two panels fire on this SHA.
    
    === #500 PASS 15 (regress only; dev_sgi_re.c untouched) ===
    
    Pass 14's pass 2 ran on nine recorded seats.  Both Opus firings died on API
    529 while the Fable seats on the other model answered, so agy was fired as
    the measuring seat -- the reservation's purpose -- and measured five
    contract-claimed families closed before its CLI timed out mid-cell; its six
    logs ARE its answer (artifacts/sgideprimop/panel14p2_agy_measured/).
    
    GAP B, two readers independently: dec regs' all-ones drawmode sets XFER_EN,
    which makes the transfer block read SIX MORE registers every session left at
    zero.  `|| step_x' MEASURED 50/50 (artifacts/sgideprimop/gapB_20260903/).
    THE PASS-14 CLOSURE OPENED IT.  Repaired by six more all-ones stores: every
    register draw_primitive() reads on a decline path is now all-ones, ELEVEN.
    
    GAP A (two readers) and a bit RELATION on op (codex): the pass-14 uncovered
    list was a per-class claim dressed as a universal.  The contract now states
    the ONLY closed shapes -- monotone bit-tests on op and the eleven registers,
    op inequality, op == 0, operand zero/nonzero -- and that everything else is
    uncovered by construction, because the sessions pin at most two values per
    field.  The NOROW summary prints the four limits.  dec regs set pins
    dst_mode too; new row dec regs stip witnesses the stipple register through
    its own channel.  Rows 50 -> 51.
    
    Table 13 (killtable_20260903_table13_xfer/): BASE 51/51; all six XFER cells
    red dec regs; M_OP_PAIRXOR and M_DRAWMODE_EQ [LIMIT] 51/51 -- escaping AS
    THE CONTRACT DECLARES; M_FLOOD_B25 control the same 3 rows.
    
    === pcc2widthkills (src/devices/dev_pcc2.c; the critical item) ===
    
    TWELVE `if (len != 1)' blocks in DEVICE_ACCESS(pcc2) ended the host on a
    guest-chosen access width -- ten fatal+exit(1) kills and two #119
    function-static latches.  Witness regress/pcc2_width_witness.py, rung 3 on
    the unmodified mvme187: 4/10 on the committed build, three aligned accesses
    each exit1, four controls green (it took three runs to be honest: run 1 was
    0/10 for the WRONG reason, `-e 187' is not a subtype alias, and the pure-RAM
    control said so).
    
    THE TREE KNEW THE WIDTH IS LEGAL: mvme_pcctworeg.h says the registers can be
    accessed as 8/16/32 bits.  So this is a DIRECTION SPLIT: READS accept (the
    memcpy above the switch already served them, raw bytes in address order,
    width-correct by construction); WRITES decline with a per-instance twelve-bit
    latch (every write arm uses `idata', which is the addressed byte ONLY at
    len==1 -- memory_readmax64 composes big-endian, so deleting the guard would
    store the NEIGHBOUR's lane).  Seven arms mask, RMW or clear on write and six
    call reassert_interrupts(), so a generic wide store cannot be right; per-lane
    COMPOSE is filed as pcc2widecompose.  Enum auto-incremented + NBITS (the fork
    records the 1<<N form as collision-prone).
    
    ALL TWELVE ARMS CONVERTED, not five: the seven odd-offset arms are
    guest-unreachable (m88k alignment check precedes memory_rw; % 0x40 keeps
    parity) but OPERATOR-reachable -- MEASURED, `put h 0xfff42003' warns, stores
    and ended the host (artifacts/pcc2widthkills/operator_reach_20260903.out).
    IPL is at 0x3e, EVEN: its #119 arm was guest-reachable and said "ignored"
    about a read that had been served.  Live exit(1): 13 -> 3, all three cited
    in the code comment (pcc2c040kill, pcc2defaultkill, interrupt_common).
    
    Detector regress/pcc2_width_probe.py, 60 rows, wired into gate_arm.sh with
    every row named and summed denominators: 4 controls; 24 survival pairs at
    the five reachable blocks; value rows (a wide read composes lanes in address
    order); readback rows (a declined write leaves BOTH lanes untouched); latch
    rows both directions; 10 accept rows (the legal width lands through each
    arm's own mask, no message); 14 operator-path rows.  ld.b/ld.h sign-extend,
    so value rows use ld.bu/ld.hu.  Every GENCTL lane value keeps bit 0x04 clear
    (pcc2c040kill).
    
    Gate 14 ARM: PASS 626 checks, 0 FAIL -- primop 51/51/0, pcc2 60/60/0 on its
    FIRST post-fix run.  Kill table (artifacts/pcc2widthkills/killtable_20260903/):
    PREFIX 14/60 (forty-six rows red); BASE 60/60; M_DELETE -> rb genctl 0xbb +
    latch rows; M_NOBREAK -> rb genctl; M_ASSIGN -> latch same; M_SHARED ->
    latch two; M_RDKILL -> both GENCTL read rows + the value row; M_OPKILL ->
    both VECBASE operator rows; M_COMPOSE -> both lane readbacks + latch rows.
    Zero clean sweeps; every prediction held.
    
    Design pass on SIX of nine (Opus x2 API 529, grok x2 CLI internal error,
    each retried once; agy reserved) plus the operator-reach measurement that
    settled its one split.  Owner asked whether to hold; default proceed.
    
    RECORDS, in the same commit: the OB row's "twelve" corrected to ten blocks /
    twelve labels in place; BOTH gate_hygiene censuses raised in step (44 -> 46,
    grandfathered 18 -> 20) for the two new pty probes -- the omission #500 pass
    11 spent two passes repairing; pcc2c040kill (HIGH, a LEGAL byte write of 0x04
    to GENCTL still ends the host) and pcc2counter8 (MED) filed from seat
    findings; clausedbound (rule question) and tablebasenotfull filed from pass
    14's panel.  check_probe_wiring.py classifies the witness, the detector and
    every artifact-side frozen copy.
    
    Build trees: dev_pcc2.c propagated to est/, build/, build-asan/; both binaries
    rebuilt; two-part clearance CLEAN/FRESH on both, est source-only, no
    sentinels.  Transport facts recorded: two panels three seconds apart 429'd
    the same Ollama seat (the spacing hazard is gone for panels minutes apart,
    not concurrent ones).
    
    Both diffs owe their own panel pass.
    
