commit b744299fbef6cd3b7ee5d7c14902edfa5a3ec548
Author:     indigoidk <indigoidk@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Aug 25 20:31:29 2026 -0500
Commit:     indigoidk <indigoidk@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Tue Aug 25 20:31:29 2026 -0500

    landiskdisk: the landisk rig now attaches a disk, and dev_wdc.c stops being untested
    
    dev_wdc.c had ZERO rig coverage in the entire battery.  The landisk rig boots a
    ramdisk with no disk image, so wdc0 attached and was never driven -- measured: not
    one ATA opcode reaches the command register across a full boot.
    
    regress/drive_guest.py
      * landisk gains an "optional_disk" key; the driver appends `-d iR:<path>` when the
        file exists and reports RIG_DISK=1/0 either way.
      * OPTIONAL BY DESIGN.  _images/ is deliberately outside the repository, so on a
        fresh clone the file is absent and the rig boots exactly as before -- but it SAYS
        SO.  A silent revert to zero wdc coverage is indistinguishable from coverage that
        ran, which is this project's silent-coverage-loss class.
    
    regress/images.md documents the image as a RECIPE, not a download:
      dd if=/dev/zero of=wdc-scratch-64m.img bs=1M count=64
    
    MEASURED, one boot on this host:
        RIG_DISK=1   BOOT_REACHED=1   VERDICT=PASS   VALUES=SH7751R,42
        wdc0 at obio0 port 0x14000000-0x1400000f
        wd0 at wdc0 channel 0 drive 0: <wdc-scratch-64m.img>
        wd0: 128-sector PIO, CHS, 64MB, 131 cyl, 16 head, 63 sec
        "Unimplemented command" warnings: 0
        image md5 IDENTICAL before and after -- R: discards guest writes, so repeated
        runs cannot inherit state
    The SH7751R,42 token gate_crossfamily.sh checks is unaffected.
    
    TWO TRAPS, carried into the code comment and images.md so they cannot be lost:
      * `-d i:R:<path>` ABORTS.  diskimage_add() takes ALL prefix chars before a SINGLE
        colon (diskimage.c:1700-1755), so the form is `-d iR:`.
      * THE DISKED BOOT RETIRES 28-34% FEWER INSTRUCTIONS in the same wall time.
        Harmless today only because landisk has "budget": 0.  A NINSTRS floor is FILED
        for this rig, and a floor derived from a diskless boot and applied to a disked
        one is a false-FAIL waiting to happen.
    
    SCOPED HONESTLY: this gives ZERO coverage of wdc_command()'s default: arm, where
    every filed wdc defect lives.  Its value is 0xF5 as wdcnoirq's witness plus general
    wdc exercise.
    
    ADJUDICATION RECORDED (fable5, on 8 of 9 seats, provisional on its face):
    
      * landiskdisk SPLITS IN TWO and only half of it ever blocked anything.  The
        probe-level -d attach belongs to wdcflood's own witness battery -- :583 is
        unreachable without a disk, so the flood measurement necessarily ran
        disk-attached and the route was already proven.  This commit is the other half.
      * wdcringambig does NOT block wdcflood.  The corrupting store is ALREADY SILENT
        today; the latch bounds repetition of a late, miscorrelated warning.
      * The pckbc-shape restructure of :145 was checked and REJECTED for a measured
        reason: it makes head==tail <=> empty sound only on the BYTE path, while the
        bulk producer can land head exactly on tail with no warning at all.  pckbc had
        one producer; wdc has three.
      * codex's repetition rule is NOT minted -- clause (d) already forces it, and two
        overlapping statements of one rule is what the carrier refuses by name.
    
    AND A WRONG RECORD OF MINE, CORRECTED.  I recorded minimax among the seats saying
    "do NOT latch :145".  It says verbatim "So: latch both."  The don't-latch camp is glm
    alone -- and glm's own fallback, downgrade to debug(), silences HARDER than the latch
    it objects to, because debug() has the early-out at core/debugmsg.c:375 and vanishes
    entirely free-running at verbose 0.  Second time in two days a seat-count in these
    records was wrong in the direction that flattered my own ruling.
    
