    #491 diskimage: two -Wsign-compare warnings were costing an entire GATE
    
    `#472` replaced `len > OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE? OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE : len` with
    `len > remain? remain : len`.  `len` is a `size_t` parameter, `remain` is `off_t`,
    and gcc warns twice at diskimage.c:1382 under the tree's own CWARNINGS.
    
    NOT A LIVE BUG, and the round says so rather than implying a data fix.
    `inblock = curofs & (OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE-1)` gives [0,511], so `remain` is in
    [1,512] and positive by construction; the conversion is value-preserving at every
    reachable value.  Both casts are provable rather than plausible.
    
    WHY IT IS A ROUND: IT WAS COSTING A GATE
    -----------------------------------------
    gate_build wants ZERO warnings, so it FAILED.  It withdraws $RIG/gxsec-gxemul at
    start and republishes ONLY on success, so gate_mips then reported
    
        mips-rigs: SKIP -- missing or non-executable binary: .../gxsec-gxemul
    
    A whole gate's coverage lost, scored as SKIP rather than FAIL.  That is
    byte-identical in shape to what one stale allowlist line cost on 2026-08-23 --
    the defect gatebuildallow records, whose summary reads "one line of text cost two
    gates."  It has now happened twice, by two routes, through the same mechanism.
    
    MEASURED -- CONTROL FIRST
    --------------------------
      reconstructed pre-fix line   rc=0  obj=44072  sign-compare=2
      shipped #491                 rc=0  obj=44112  sign-compare=0
    
    Then the cascade, which is the claim that actually matters:
    
      BEFORE       arc rig binary ABSENT -- withdrawn by the failed battery run
      gate_build   ok pmax: warnings 0 / ok arc: warnings 0 / PASS (18 checks)
      republished  gxsec-gxemul 6155864 b
      gate_mips    mips-rigs: PASS (6 checks)          <- was SKIP
    
    The ABSENT row is the control: it shows the binary really had been withdrawn, so
    the republication is attributable rather than assumed.
    
    *** MY FIRST VERIFICATION WAS VACUOUS AND ITS OWN CONTROL CAUGHT IT. ***  It
    reported 0 warnings for the PRE-FIX form, which must be 2.  The compile was
    failing on a missing include and the script read its empty output as a result --
    the phantom-absence class, inside a script written to prove a fix.  Take 2 prints
    compile rc and object size BEFORE the warning count and refuses to read the count
    without them.  Without the control, "post-fix = 0" would have shipped as proof.
    
    HOW IT SURVIVED TWO DAYS
    -------------------------
    Warnings need a BUILD; builds are too slow for precommit; so warnings are checked
    only by the weekly battery.  A warning-introducing commit is invisible for up to
    seven days, and only surfaces then if someone READS the result.  The battery had
    been RED since 2026-08-23 on an unrelated stale allowlist entry, and
    nightly_check.sh cannot distinguish "fixed" from "never looked at" -- so this sat
    behind a red everyone already had an explanation for.  #472's own round is not at
    fault: the per-commit targeted gate is narrow by design.
    
    ALSO IN THIS COMMIT
    --------------------
    * #490's PASS-2 RECEIPT, marked partial on one named axis: the detector was
      UNTRACKED at panel time, so the seats read a file git could not see.  Recorded
      per 84765ec's precedent, which refused the same stretch.
    * propagatecpsilent -- the propagate script prints "propagated" after a FAILED
      cp.  A claim of ACTION at the moment of failure, the same shape as panel.sh
      announcing "re-firing once" while re-firing nothing.  The two-part clearance
      CONTAINED it (part 1 NO, sentinel KEPT), so the tree was marked untrustworthy
      rather than silently wrong.
    * batteryblindstart -- the battery's pre-flight git status is a ~15-MINUTE window
      (16:06:12 fired, START=16:21:09) in which no log and no verdict exist, so the
      carrier's redirect-target rule gives the WRONG answer and an orphaned start is
      indistinguishable from a healthy one.
    * The five remaining battery reds are FILED, not fixed: two are not simple
      re-pins.  `whole-buffer full-prompt` is a fail-closed allowlist over a pattern
      #392 measured at 0/80 and must NOT be raised; `wdcflood: six warned_ guards`
      needs equality->floor plus an L4 correction, its comment having claimed
      immunity to the growth that just broke it.
    
    All three build trees propagated AND rebuilt, two-part clearance re-derived from
    disk.  PRECOMMIT_PASS 0 hard, 4 soft.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

