    seatthinkburn: two more instances, and the burn tracks the BRIEF rather than the seat
    
    The carrier said this fifth seat-failure class "was never written up here -- the
    hole is in this file, not in the count.  Filed, not lost."  It is written up now,
    because today produced two fresh instances AND a correlation the row did not have.
    
        panel_20260826_090604    4,032 b   normal      simple brief
        panel_20260826_190055    2,845 b   normal      simple brief
        panel_20260826_222557  142,525 b   BURNED      three-claim band-arithmetic audit
        panel_20260826_230207  222,981 b   BURNED      five questions across two rounds
    
    SAME SEAT, SAME TRANSPORT, SAME DAY.  The burns track BRIEF COMPLEXITY.
    
    *** THAT REFRAMES THE CLASS AND CHANGES THE REMEDY. ***  The row recorded it as a
    SEAT property -- something to detect and work around.  It is at least partly a
    BRIEF property, which is actionable in a way a seat outage is not: I CAN SHORTEN
    THE BRIEF.  And it is the carrier's oldest packet-fed lesson recurring -- their
    behaviour is governed by the brief, and this project once spent DAYS misdiagnosing
    a brief defect as a seat outage.
    
    WHAT IS LOST IS NOT NOISE.  The second burn ends mid-sentence -- "So verdict likely
    NOT RATIFY due to #467.  But maybe the question is from a panel" -- IT HAD REACHED
