                            "note":  "(HELD-AWAITING-SEAT codex -- DEFANGED 2026-08-29: that seat ANSWERED on 2026-08-26, see its entry of that date.  The literal marker is broken on purpose because three tools read it functionally and a stale one makes an answered stage report as waiting.) QUOTA WALL, fourth consecutive panel, payload 688 bytes over the brief -- the same signature every time. Re-fire after Aug 22.  [panel_20260818_095322]"
                        },
                        {
                            "phase":  "review",
                            "seat":  "grok",
                            "date":  "2026-08-18",
                            "verdict":  "REAL",
                            "evidence":  "MANUAL",
                            "note":  "*** REACHED THE PASS-2 HEADLINE INDEPENDENTLY, from reading alone: \u0027Overlay rows\u0027 names overclaim. They count calls, not targets\u0027 and \u0027DO NOT SHIP THE DETECTOR AS EVIDENCE OF (b) UNTIL THE WRAP NAMES THE FD.\u0027 *** The measure seat proved the same thing with four mutants; grok saw it in the source. It also prescribed the exact read-only fix that was adopted -- \u0027if nr_of_overlays==0 \u0026\u0026 !d-\u003ewritable, return 1 without touching the stream\u0027 -- and found TWO comment defects nobody else did: the new comment said diskimage_scsicmd.cc when the file is .c, and MY PATCH HAD INSERTED diskimage_sync() BETWEEN diskimage_dump_info()\u0027s DOC COMMENT AND ITS BODY, orphaning that comment above an unrelated function -- my anchor was the signature, and a signature is not the top of a function when a doc block precedes it. Both fixed. Siblings it filed rather than chased: START STOP UNIT, SYNCHRONIZE CACHE(16) 0x91, WDCC_FLUSHCACHE.  [panel_20260818_095322]"
                        },
                        {
                            "phase":  "regress",
                            "seat":  "fable5",
                            "date":  "2026-08-19",
                            "verdict":  "REAL",
                            "evidence":  "CONFIRMED",
                            "note":  "FABLE REGRESS ADJUDICATION of verdict_20260819_135703 at 6014b7e. Badge `s` disclosed: same-model adjudication of the main loop\u0027s records, not a two-family check.\n* *** Q2 REFUTED MY OWN SUSPICION USING THE BATTERY\u0027S OWN LOG. *** I wrote that no gate asserts the guest-visible CHECK CONDITION. Lines 554 and 559 say otherwise (verified here): `overlay: a failed sync reports CHECK CONDITION 2` and `nothing open: sync reports CHECK CONDITION, not GOOD 2` -- FAULT-INJECTED via fail_fsync_fd returning EIO, driven through the real diskimage_scsicommand() with a WRITE(10)-then-SYNCHRONIZE-CACHE CDB pair, not a direct call. So gate 2 EXERCISED the changed path discriminatingly rather than merely not breaking on it. The live gates ran the success leg for real: luna88k reached login in gates 5 and 7.\n* Q1 MY FRAMING WAS WRONG IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Too strong: the battery is NOT the evidence the harness commits did not break the emulator -- GIT IS. `git diff --name-only 1ba2cd4..6014b7e` minus regress/tools/docs leaves exactly the three #437 files, so no build input outside #437 changed and the harness commits COULD NOT have altered the binary. Too weak: the 16/16 IS evidence about those commits -- it is the first end-to-end execution of their product, 16/16 with 0 skipped means no gate silently dropped out, and the selfmutant controls DETECTED in this run.\n* AND A FRAMING ERROR I REPEATED TWICE TODAY: diskimage_sync() does NOT sit on a path \u0027every rig\u0027s disk traffic crosses\u0027. ONLY command 0x35 reaches it; ordinary READ/WRITE cross diskimage_scsicommand() but not the sync handler. The blast radius is narrower than I said.\n* #437 touched THREE src/ files, not one: diskimage.c, diskimage_scsicmd.c, diskimage.h. \u0027One src/ COMMIT\u0027 was true; the round record should name the three files.\n* Q3 NO EMERGENCY RE-RUN for 20ce22e and 7e3b120 -- every changed line is gate 2\u0027s surface or non-battery tooling, and the binary is bit-identical by construction, so a full battery would re-measure 14 unchanged gates against an unchanged binary: ritual, not evidence. ONE CHEAP CONDITION: selftest_mutation.sh\u0027s own header says run it after any change to gate 2, and that rule was triggered. Run gate 3 once at HEAD.\n* Q4 VACUITY, NAMED NOT SURVEYED: (1) gate_asan_sweep is a CONSTRUCTION sweep -- 37 machine types construct under ASan and nothing more, so *** #437\u0027s NEW CODE HAS NEVER RUN UNDER ASan ***; (2) gate_hygiene\u0027s pattern set contains ZERO occurrences of sync/sense/sd0, so the new guest-visible error class is invisible to it; (3) gate_arm passed 16/16 WITH armbdt PRESENT -- not hypothetical, the measured LDM/STM defect was live at this HEAD; (4) selftest_mutation\u0027s green means ONE differential of eleven can fail, and its apparatus carries smhang/smnotland unfixed; (5) gate_ab is coarse rather than vacuous -- marker parity 1:1:1 accepted ~0.44% instruction drift. CHECKED CLEAN: gate_upstream\u0027s empty-both-sides hole is closed, gate 5 carries mutant-derived NINSTRS floors, and the old prompt-predicate hole in arm_flags_probe.py is CLOSED (its own 7-day-old memory note claiming otherwise is stale).\n* Q5 QUEUE RISK THE BATTERY CANNOT SEE, ranked: armbdt (the only MEASURED defect, battery structurally green over it); idesync (the #437 CLASS on the other disk stack, and the ATA rig boots a ramdisk kernel that issues no flush traffic); b120r; the four wdc residuals including a guest-set malloc count behind CHECK_ALLOCATION; the three selfmutant apparatus items; and m437multi carries INVERTED risk -- the battery now PINS the conservative behaviour that item wants changed, so its fix round must expect a SCHEDULED RED, not a regression."
                        },
                        {
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "seat":  "fable5",
                            "date":  "2026-08-19",
