                            "date":  "2026-08-26",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/brief_wdcflood_final_opus.md (final-diff read; no build -- a kill table was running)",
                            "note":  "FINAL DIFF, FIRED AFTER PASS 2 TO CLOSE THE ROSTER GAP -- and it found what two panels and three adjudications had not. **VERDICT: SHIP THE CODE; the CONTRACT carries a third non-sequitur and it is load-bearing.** Read-only by instruction (a table was mid-run); it said so plainly and named the four mutants it would want instead of guessing. *** THE FINDING: MY CONTRACT WARRANTED FLAG-PAIRING SURVIVAL ON \u0027every row starts a FRESH emulator ... proving per-instance storage needs TWO controller instances, which this rig does not have\u0027. THAT EXPLAINS THE PROCESS-GLOBAL CASE ONLY. *** Pairing survived because **NO ROW FIRES TWO DIFFERENT SITES IN ONE SESSION** -- a property of the ROW SET, not the rig, and fixable in three lines. It checked all 22 rows to confirm zero did (datawr x2 writes wd_data so the width check is never reached; overrun x2 uses legal 8-bit writes; both value rows seed and read 8-bit). **AN UNMEASURABLE CLAIM WAS HIDING A MEASURABLE ONE BEHIND IT** -- and the measurable half is the round\u0027s HEADLINE design decision. Shipped as `wr indep`. *** AND THE PER-INSTANCE HALF IS NOT IMPOSSIBLE EITHER -- \u0027this rig does not have\u0027 is true of landisk and FALSE OF THE FORK: *** `dev_pcic.c:234-242` adds TWO wdc instances unconditionally (0x14000180 and 0x140001f0; its own comment reads \u0027Yuck. Now there are two.\u0027), reached from every hpcmips subtype. Verified. So that is COVERAGE DEBT, not an impossibility, and the contract now says which. *** A SIBLING-PARITY GAP IN THE CARRIER\u0027S EXACT SENSE. *** `w16 reset` covers reset-on-normal-operation at :607 **BY ACCIDENT** -- it happens to place a legal 8-bit write between its two wide writes. Its mirror at :1025 had nothing: r16 x2 and r32 x2 fire back-to-back, r16 value seeds with a WRITE and checks values not counts, accept r8 is a separate session. So `d-\u003ewarned_nonbyte_read = 0;` on a legal 8-bit read scored **22/22**. Same predicate, same message modulo WRITE/READ, added in the same hunk pair. Shipped as `r16 reset`. *** A SECOND ESCAPE FROM THE GUARD-FIELD/BODY-FIELD CHECK, VERIFIED BY READING: *** :583\u0027s guard reads `warned_unimpl_cmd` (:655) while its BODY reads `d-\u003eseccnt` (:660), a field the guest writes directly at :1003 and nothing else touches. So `if (!d-\u003eseccnt) { d-\u003eseccnt = 1; ... }` there scores a clean sweep, and no row builds a state where the two fields disagree. FILED. *** TWO CONTRACT BULLETS WERE UNSCOPED -- listed under DESIGNED TO CATCH while each was measured at exactly ONE site of six. *** Reset-on-normal was pinned only at :583; guest-resettable-operand only at :607. **A capability claimed generally and measured once is the overclaim the contract exists to prevent.** Both now name their pinned sites and their unpinned ones. *** THE SUBTLEST CATCH: A WRONG CITATION THAT LOOKS RIGHT. *** `dev_wdc.c:89` cited the shared #337 flag as spanning \u0027:709 vs its else\u0027. The round uses PRE-FIX numbering throughout and that convention is otherwise applied correctly -- the seat checked HEAD and withdrew its own wrong-citation finding on the others. But :89 is the ONE citation that ships INSIDE the file it points into, where a reader resolves it against the POST-FIX copy -- and post-fix :709 is `odata = (odata \u003c\u003c 8) + wdc_get_inbuf(d);`, an inbuf line inside an endianness conditional, **which reads like a confirmation**. Replaced with a positional reference. IT ALSO STRENGTHENED THE :145 ARGUMENT RATHER THAN WEAKENING IT: the announcement was never a corruption detector to begin with, because the FAST BULK PATH laps the ring by direct pointer arithmetic without ever calling `wdc_addtoinbuf`, so it never announced there at all. That is a better warrant than \u0027the latch bounds the announcement\u0027. AND IT RE-DERIVED TWO ARITHMETIC CLAIMS INDEPENDENTLY: 1026 x 512 = 525,312 = exactly 2 laps of WDC_INBUF_SIZE; and \u0027500 iterations -\u003e 2000 lines\u0027 falls out of the file, because a 32-bit read of wd_data calls `wdc_get_inbuf()` FOUR times. The round never stated that derivation; it corroborates the measurement from the source side. CENSUS CONFIRMED AGAINST THE FILE: exactly ten `fatal(\"` call sites, four #337\u0027s and six this round\u0027s; the two `printf()` at :391/:437 are inside `#if 0` and correctly excluded. Both gate pins verified by grep (10 and 12). All six guards wrap the announcement ONLY -- checked line by line. No latch is guest-clearable: `memset(d, 0, ...)` occurs once, in DEVINIT."
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "opus5",
                            "phase":  "review",
                            "d":  "�o"",
                            "date":  "2026-08-26",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/brief_wdcflood_askagain.md (THE ONE PERMITTED ASK-AGAIN; reasoned, not built -- a table was running)",
                            "note":  "*** THE CAPPED ASK-AGAIN, FIRED AGAINST A DETECTOR ALREADY CLEAN AT 24 ROWS -- AND IT FOUND ONE. *** Rule satisfied: found -\u003e ONE row under L1 -\u003e cap SPENT, no second query. **THE MUTANT: key the :607 latch on the ACCESS WIDTH instead of on a boolean.** `if (len != 1 \u0026\u0026 d-\u003ewarned_nonbyte_write != (int) len) { d-\u003ewarned_nonbyte_write = (int) len;` -- two lines, one hunk. A guest alternating `mov.w` / `mov.l` at wd_seccnt then gets ONE HOST LINE PER STORE, FOREVER: flag 0 != 2 -\u003e line, flag = 2; flag 2 != 4 -\u003e line, flag = 4; flag 4 != 2 -\u003e line ... That is the pre-fix rate this round measured at 20 stores -\u003e 20 lines. *** WHY NO ROW COULD SEE IT: 2 AND 4 NEVER CO-OCCUR IN A SINGLE SESSION. *** `w16 x2` fires (2,2); `w32 x2` fires (4,4); they are SEPARATE sessions. The reset rows interpose a `len == 1` access, which `len != 1` rejects BEFORE the flag operand is consulted, so they cannot re-key it. The seat walked all 24 sessions and tabulated the multiset of `len` values reaching each guard per session -- mechanically, not by eye. **:607 is the MOST heavily covered site in the file (six rows aim at it) and all six stay green**, which is what makes this a demonstration rather than a blunt break. **IT IS THE SAME CLASS THE ROUND ALREADY DECLARED A DEFECT AT :583** -- `warned_unimpl_cmd != cur_command`, killed by `unimpl 2op` -- transposed to a site where nothing could observe it. And it is a PLAUSIBLE maintainer edit, not an adversarial one: \u0027report each distinct bad width once\u0027 is natural, and :704\u0027s message prints `len=%i`, which invites it. *** THE GENERALISATION IS WORTH MORE THAN THE MUTANT, and it is one grep: *** the contract already asks *do two SITES share a session?* (`wr indep`). **Its DUAL was missing -- *for each site, does any ONE session present two DIFFERENT stimuli that both reach that site\u0027s guard?*** :583 yes (two opcodes); :607, :1025, :704, :160 and :145 all repeated an IDENTICAL stimulus. That is why the whole last-value-latch family sat unpinned at five sites of six. Closed at the two width sites by `w mixed` / `r mixed`; :704 remains open and is now named in the contract. *** AND IT REFUTED A CONTRACT LINE I HAD WRITTEN THAT SAME HOUR. *** I claimed reset-on-normal-operation was \u0027pinned at :583 (`interleave`)\u0027. **VERIFIED FALSE IN SCOPE: `interleave`\u0027s only valid opcode is 0xEC, against NINETEEN valid command cases** -- so the recorded kill covers one case in nineteen, and a reset hidden in `WDCC_RECAL`, `SET_FEATURES` or `WDCC_DIAGNOSE` sweeps clean. **Worse, a reset arriving through the SIBLING HANDLER is pinned NOWHERE**: `dev_wdc_altstatus_access` shares the same `d`, and zero rows in this file touch its address -- which is where a real driver\u0027s reset goes. Both verified by grep and both now scoped in the contract; filed as `wdcflagindep`. *** THE SEAT FLAGGED ITS OWN POSSIBLE RE-PROPOSAL RATHER THAN CLAIMING NOVELTY, AND THE REASON IS A DEFECT IN MY BRIEF: *** it could not tell whether the other-opcode reset was already covered, because **my exclusion list gave LABELS, not EDITS** -- the exact defect that same brief warned about two paragraphs earlier (\u0027a seat once conflated two mutants because a brief showed labels only, and that was the brief\u0027s defect\u0027). It said so plainly and left the call to me. *An exclusion list is a brief too, and it earns the same standard as the rest of one.* SCOPE OFFERED, NOT PROPOSED (all REASONED, none the headline): :704 takes the same edit and sweeps clean; keying it on `idata` is worse and also sweeps clean, since `datawr x2` writes 0x1234 both times. METHOD: read-only by instruction -- a kill table was running and its rows use fixed 8-second settle windows. It read all 1187 lines of dev_wdc.c, all 557 of the probe, `memory.h:149` for `len`\u0027s type, and `wdcreg.h`; it labelled the finding REASONED and stated plainly it had not verified the mutant compiles. **The mutant\u0027s PREMISE is already measured, not assumed**: this round\u0027s own `len != 1` -\u003e `len == 2` mutant is recorded as killing `w32 x2`/`r32 x2` ALONE, which measures that `len == 4` reaches the guard as a distinct value while `len == 2` leaves the 16-bit rows green. Only the control flow over the flag is reasoned, and it is four lines of straight-line C."
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "fable5",
                            "phase":  "review",
                            "d":  "�o"",
                            "date":  "2026-08-26",
                            "badge":  "s",
                            "ev":  "Agent(model=fable) READINESS ADJUDICATION of the final artifacts; liveness token FABLE_ADJ_ALIVE_20260826C returned. NO panel dir -- an Agent seat leaves no file, which is the counting trap the carrier records.",
                            "note":  "*** DUAL HAT DISCLOSED: this is the fable5 SEAT read of the final artifacts AND the adjudication, held by one model. Badged `s`. It is recorded as ONE seat, never as two, and the seat-vs-adjudicator distinction the carrier draws is NOT satisfied by this entry alone. *** VERDICT: SHIP-WITH -- floor holds, seven bounded items before commit. EVIDENCE BASIS, stated on its face and therefore PROVISIONAL: every artifact on disk at read time -- five table dirs, 37 raw logs then extant, 8 results files, the probe, the dev_wdc.c diff, the gate diff, the ledger, both frozen table-5 scripts, the witness dir, three checker runs. It ran nothing heavier than sub-second read-only checkers, by choice, because a kill table was live. *** THE FIRST ITEM WAS A HARD CHECKER FAIL THE ROUND WOULD HAVE HIT AT PRECOMMIT: *** `check_bugfile_sync.py` reported BUGFILE_SYNC_FAIL on four open rows -- `wdcperopcode`, `wdcexpecteddata`, `wdcflagindep`, `wdchpcmipsaddr` -- filed in the ledger and absent from OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md. **The checker THIS ROUND repaired for exactly that shape caught the round that repaired it.** Written; now BUGFILE_SYNC_PASS. SEVEN ITEMS AND THEIR DISPOSITION, all closed except the gate run: (1) four bug-file entries -- WRITTEN, PASS. (2) the pre-fix line-number convention was claimed and ABSENT from the probe -- WRITTEN, and then immediately re-keyed: the post-fix NUMERIC column went stale ONE EDIT LATER when a six-line comment moved all six sites by four, so the map now keys on the FLAG NAME, which cannot rot. (3) clause (c) was measured at 22 rows and the shipped script is 26 -- RE-MEASURED: 0/26 on both media, 26 FAIL, zero survivors (table6_null26/). The floor was satisfied either way; the sentence \u0027every row fails\u0027 was unmeasured for four rows and now is not. (4) the gate comment said THE DENOMINATOR IS 22 above a check pinning 26 -- CORRECTED to 26 and TWELVE, with the four new rows named. (5) the witness artifacts lived in a VOLATILE session scratchpad the ledger cited -- COPIED to regress/artifacts/wdcflood/witness_20260825/ and the witness field re-pointed. n3.out is byte-identical after copy and is exactly 158,449 bytes, the figure three records cite. (6) the no-disk `debug()` sibling that the ORIGINAL FILING named was disposed of NOWHERE -- now named in the round block and the gate comment, as OUTSIDE scope rather than missed: `debug()` has the early-out `fatal()` lacks, so -q silences it. Different channel, different remedy; rides with `floodclass`. (7) one clean run of the never-executed gate section -- PENDING, post-table. *** IT ALSO CAUGHT FOUR DEFECTS IN THE ROUND BLOCK DRAFT, AND TWO OF THEM I HAD ALREADY FOUND BY AUDITING THE DRAFT AGAINST ITS OWN ARTIFACTS -- independent convergence, not duplication. *** (a) \u0027SIX stamped directories\u0027 when there were five -- an error I INTRODUCED while filling slots, the second time this round a CORRECTION carried an error; (b) \u0027the eight rows added after the pre-fix run\u0027 is TWELVE, a sentence true at 22 rows that went stale when the detector grew -- the same class as the gate comment; (c) **\u0027ALL 26 with a measured kill\u0027 OVERCLAIMS by this project\u0027s own usage of \u0027kill\u0027** -- measured 23+3: `live`, `accept w8` and `accept r8` redden ONLY on a null medium, and the draft should not be looser than the probe it describes; (d) the pre-fix flood numbers cited no artifact and their artifacts were about to evaporate. *** AND ONE OMISSION THAT WOULD HAVE BURIED A SIBLING: *** see item 6. Closing `wdcflood` as-drafted would have closed a queue id whose own filing named a defect the round neither fixed nor filed. ON Q2, THE CLAUSE-(b) MAPPING\u0027S HOME: the probe header is primary and the round block owes only the pointer -- do NOT duplicate the six-line table into the CHANGELOG, because a second copy nothing checks is the antipattern the carrier documents twice. Followed. ON Q3, THE ASK-AGAIN CAP: confirmed spent -- found, two rows under L1, both mutants measured killed, so the L1 obligation is discharged BY KILLS and not by rows existing. **Its boundary is worth keeping: the cap governs the HUNT. The clause-(c) re-run, the record corrections and the bug-file sync are floor and record obligations, which the cap neither covers nor excuses.** A MEASUREMENT IT CORRECTED IN MY FAVOUR: table 5 was further along than CHECKPOINT.md said -- `Mwidr` had already landed and killed (25/26, RED `r mixed` alone), so an \u0027assume it kills\u0027 in my own question was already measured. AND ONE PIECE OF HOUSEKEEPING WORTH THE LINE: it spent real effort ruling out a silently lost mutant before concluding **there is no Mp2** -- the numbering always went Mp1/Mp3/Mp4. One sentence now in the round block spares the next reader the same search."
