                            "note":  "FILE-READING, and it opened the right tree -- it names the six post-fix guards at 194, 220, 661, 689, 791, 1118 and says explicitly \u0027not another tree\u0027. CONFIRMED, each against source: the dev_asc warrant holds (fatal() always reaches va_debug; debug() alone has the early-out at debugmsg.c:365/:375); **every guest-visible effect remains outside its guard**, enumerated one by one -- ring store and head advancement precede the overrun guard, `return (uint64_t)-1` is outside the over-read latch, WDCE_ABRT precedes the unimplemented-command latch, `idata = data[0]` follows the write-width latch, unexpected-DATA processing continues after its latch, and `data[0] = odata` with `return 1` stay in the common tail -- **\u0027no early-return regression was introduced\u0027**, which is the exact hazard the sketch rule exists for. *** IT RATIFIED THE ROUND\u0027S DE-ESCALATION READING, WHICH WAS THE QUESTION MOST LIKELY TO MAKE THE RECORD FALSE: *** the clause fires when a fix REMOVES a host-fatal guard; these fatal() calls never terminated the host and none was removed, so `live`, `accept w8` and `accept r8` do NOT owe product-code kills and their null-medium reds satisfy non-vacuity. The round block said exactly this; it is now ratified by a seat that checked the clause text. TWO FINDINGS ACTED ON: (1) **[P2] a smaller escape** -- one line, `d-\u003ewarned_nonbyte_write = 0;` in the wd_sector write arm -- source-proven to leave all 26 rows green while producing an unbounded flood. FILED as `wdcsectorreset` rather than fixed, because the seat itself labelled it un-measured. (2) **an L4 wrong record**: the round said the no-disk sibling \u0027floods identically\u0027; codex re-derived from debugmsg.c that it is silent free-running at default verbosity, so \u0027identically\u0027 should mean identical REPETITION when the debug channel is enabled, not identical VISIBILITY. Corrected in place. *** AND THE CORRECTION\u0027S PROVENANCE IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING: the qualifier was NOT missing from the evidence, it was missing from my summary. *** OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md\u0027s original filing already read \u0027invisible free-running at verbosity 0\u0027. I kept the headline and dropped the scope -- the MIRROR of the silent-narrowing failure the carrier records, and it survives every check except comparing a summary against its source. It also held the line on flag pairing: `wr indep` proves only that the two WIDTH flags cannot share; ring-half sharing still passes and other cross-site sharing has no co-firing row. That is `wdcflagindep`, already filed, and the round may not claim more than it measured."
