                            "note":  "*** #486 REPAIRED THIS ROUND\u0027S OWN CLAUSE-(b) CARRIER, WHICH HAD BEEN NON-DISCRIMINATING. ***\n\n`overrun x2` is #464\u0027s sole clause-(b) carrier at the ring producer.  MEASURED on the\ncommitted binary before #486: it reads OVERRUN = 0 on the shipped latch AND 0 on a build with\nthe latch DELETED.  Not merely red -- it could not tell the fix from its absence, so #464\u0027s\nfloor was open at that site with nothing saying so.\n\n#479 killed it: an unconditional `wdc_new_command_reset()` capped per-command occupancy at\n512, so 1026 IDENTIFY commands could no longer lap a 262,656-byte ring.  Proven by a\nsingle-variable control -- revert only that reset, keep #484\u0027s ring, and OVERRUN goes 0 -\u003e 1.\n\n#486 re-aimed the stimulus at the guest data port, which takes no command and therefore no\nreset.  Now: shipped 1,1,0 ok; latch deleted 1,145,0 FAIL.  Probe 25/26 -\u003e 26/26, with the\ngate\u0027s pinned row count unchanged at 26.\n\nThe commit is named here because work shipped for this row and a row that does not name its\ncommit cannot be traced back from the log -- the gate refused the next commit until it did."
