                            "note":  "*** THE \u002710 REAL OPCODES\u0027 FIGURE IS MEASURED FALSE, AND THE CORRECTION REMOVES THIS ROW\u0027S STATED VALUE. ***  Booted with the exact rig args plus a disk: 14 command-register writes across SEVEN opcodes to the installer prompt --\n    3x 0xEC IDENTIFY  3x 0x20 READ  2x 0xC6 SETMULTI  2x 0x91 IDP\n    2x 0x10 RECAL     1x 0xF5 SEC_FREEZE_LOCK        1x 0xC4 READMULTI\n    \"Unimplemented command\" warnings: 0\nNo 0xE0, no 0x30 WRITE, no 0xC5 WRITEMULTI -- those come from a full filesystem lifecycle through halt -p, which this rig never performs. Grok predicted this from reading; it is now measured. *** CONSEQUENCE: adding -d i: gives ZERO coverage of the default: arm -- the arm all four defect rows live in. ***  Its real value is as [[wdcnoirq]]\u0027s rung-4 witness via 0xF5, which is a different and smaller claim.\n\nSAFE TO ADD -- measured, fixed 25 s windows, same host and binary:\n    no disk         prompt_reached=1  instrs=2,852,727,965\n    iR: 64MB blank  prompt_reached=1  instrs=1,879,394,907\n    no disk    (2)  prompt_reached=1  instrs=2,382,496,189\n    iR: 64MB   (2)  prompt_reached=1  instrs=1,711,379,982\nBoth reach the installer menu; wd0 attaches and is probed; gate_crossfamily.sh\u0027s SH7751R,42 token is unaffected; the installer waits rather than auto-installing.\n\n*** TWO TRAPS. (1) SYNTAX: `-d i:R:\u003cpath\u003e` ABORTS *** (diskimage_add(): invalid prefix char -- the parser at diskimage.c:1700-1755 takes all prefix chars before a SINGLE colon). The correct form is `-d iR:\u003cpath\u003e`. Getting this wrong is exactly the \u0027latently red for two commits\u0027 shape. *** (2) THE DISK CONFIG RETIRES 28-34% FEWER INSTRUCTIONS IN THE SAME WALL TIME. ***  Harmless today only because drive_guest.py:84 sets \"budget\": 0 -- landisk deliberately has no instruction ceiling. But its own comment says a NINSTRS floor is FILED, and *** a floor derived from today\u0027s diskless boot and applied to a disked one is a false-FAIL waiting to happen. ***  Also: the base image must be R:-prefixed or the guest writes the shared rig image, and the installer prompt has NO TRAILING NEWLINE, which is why the rig needs drive_guest.py\u0027s pty predicate rather than line-oriented matching.",
