        "state_note":  "  *** COMMITS FIELD FILLED 2026-08-26: `b744299` shipped this row\u0027s work and the row did not name it, so section L hard-failed the NEXT commit -- correctly. The gate is doing exactly its job: it caught a records gap left by the previous round, not by this one. b744299 changed regress/drive_guest.py (+57, the landisk rig now attaches `wdc-scratch-64m.img` via `-d iR:` and prints RIG_DISK=1/0), regress/images.md (+41, the dd recipe, since the image is generated and not downloaded), and the ledger/matrix pair. The row stays `in work` rather than closing: the disk half shipped, and this row was split in two by adjudication -- see below. ***\n  *** SPLIT IN TWO BY ADJUDICATION 2026-08-25, AND HALF OF IT IS DONE. *** This row was ranked as a BLOCKER on four other rows\u0027 witnesses. It is really two deliverables and only one of them ever blocked anything. **HALF A -- the PROBE-level attach. NOT A BLOCKER, and it was already proven:** :583 is unreachable without a disk (dev_wdc.c:461-468 early-returns), so the opus5 flood measurement necessarily ran disk-attached. A witness battery can attach its own disk; it does not need the rig. **HALF B -- the BATTERY-RIG integration. SHIPPED 2026-08-25 and verified by a boot.** `_images/wdc-scratch-64m.img` is 67,108,864 bytes of zeros, generated not downloaded (recipe in `regress/images.md`). `drive_guest.py` gained an `optional_disk` key and appends `-d iR:\u003cpath\u003e` when the file exists. **MEASURED on this host, one boot:** RIG_DISK=1, BOOT_REACHED=1, VERDICT=PASS, VALUES=SH7751R,42 (the token gate_crossfamily checks, unaffected), zero \"Unimplemented command\" warnings, **and the image md5 IDENTICAL before and after -- so `R:` is discarding guest writes as intended and repeated runs cannot inherit state.** **OPTIONAL BY DESIGN AND IT SAYS SO.** `_images/` is deliberately outside the repository, so on a fresh clone the file is absent; the rig then boots exactly as before and prints `RIG_DISK=0 absent:\u003cpath\u003e`. That report is the point -- a silent revert to zero wdc coverage is indistinguishable from coverage that ran, which is this project\u0027s silent-coverage-loss class. **THE NINSTRS POISON IS THE PART THAT STILL MATTERS AND IT IS UNCHANGED:** the disked boot retires 28-34% fewer instructions in the same wall time. Harmless today only because drive_guest.py sets \"budget\": 0 for landisk. A NINSTRS floor is FILED for this rig, and a floor derived from a diskless boot and applied to a disked one is a false-FAIL waiting to happen -- whoever calibrates it must calibrate the DISKED config. Carried into the code comment and into images.md so it cannot be lost. **SCOPE IT HONESTLY: this gives ZERO coverage of wdc_command()\u0027s `default:` arm**, which is where every filed wdc defect lives. Its real value is 0xF5 SEC_FREEZE_LOCK as `wdcnoirq`\u0027s witness plus general wdc exercise."
