                            "note":  "ADJUDICATOR CONTRIBUTION TO THIS ROUND -- recorded as what it is, not dressed up as a panel seat\u0027s brief answer. Fable held the ADJUDICATOR hat on 2026-08-20 and its docket opened with this round: \u0027Item 0 -- land the in-flight pitlatch+pitclobber round; do not contend.\u0027\n\n*** AND IT MADE ONE SUBSTANTIVE CORRECTION THAT CHANGED THIS ROW\u0027S RECORD: *** \u0027the PIT panel\u0027s \"no merges, five rounds\" ruling PREDATES pitclobber (filed after that panel). The pairing is therefore UN-RULED, not ruled-against -- the round record must justify it explicitly under the third-arm test (same device, same LATCH-command semantic class, one fix design). It plausibly passes; it must say so.\u0027\n\nThat was right and I had it wrong: I told the driving seat \u0027the panel folded pitclobber in\u0027. The CLUSTER panel never saw pitclobber; the pitlatch DESIGN panel did, because I wrote the write-side clobber into that brief myself. The justification exists -- from the design panel, not the cluster panel -- and the closure note now says which.\n\nNOT a substitute for a fable5 review of the diff. The regress review remains FABLE-ONLY and is held and queued below.",
