                            "date":  "2026-08-20",
                            "note":  "PASS 2 ON #439 -- 7 OF 7 SCRIPTABLE SEATS, THE FIRST FULL SCRIPTABLE PANEL OF THIS CAMPAIGN. Codex answered for real (20,699 bytes) after ten consecutive echo-only walls.\n\n*** SIX SEATS SOUND; CODEX DEFECTIVE -- AND CODEX WAS RIGHT. ***  \u0027The latch is never consumed, so the selected counter returns zero indefinitely.\u0027 Verified in source: latched[] is SET at :212, cleared ONLY at :219 by a non-latch mode write, and NEVER cleared by the read at :163. After one latch command, every subsequent read of that counter returns 0 until the guest happens to rewrite the mode byte. A real 8254 CONSUMES the latch per the programmed RW format.\n\nThe seat that had been WALLED for the pass-1 panel is the one that found it, which is the clearest argument this campaign has produced for discharging a wall rather than recording it and moving on. glm gestured at the same thing (\u0027the sticky latch\u0027).\n\nNOT A REGRESSION: pre-#439 a latch clobbered mode_byte and subsequent reads also fell to the default arm returning 0, plus an unsilenceable flood. But it is a real defect in the fix, and SHIP-WITH-FIX is this project\u0027s practice on a pass-2 finding.\n\nHANDED TO THE IN-FLIGHT pitflip ROUND rather than fixed separately, and the reason is technical not merely practical: the consume semantics INTERACT WITH THE LSB/MSB FLIP-FLOP. In 16-bit mode a real latch delivers TWO bytes before reverting -- and the selector is exactly what pitflip is fixing. Two rounds editing dev_8253.c at once would also contend.\n\nTHE REFUSAL OF THE PASS-1 MAJORITY IS VINDICATED. The six SOUND verdicts converged on the brief\u0027s substantive question -- agy: \u0027returning 0 avoids guest kernel divide-by-zero crashes, preserves programmed mode state\u0027; deepseek: \u0027the least harmful of three wrong answers and not a guest-visible regression\u0027; minimax: \u0027the write-side fix matches the 8254 and removes a real bug\u0027. Nobody defended the reload-value design that the implementing seat built and measured harmful. What was missed by everyone, including me, was the consume.",
