                            "note":  "SOUND -- \u0027returning 0 avoids guest kernel divide-by-zero crashes, preserves programmed mode state, and cleanly silences the false error.\u0027 A FILE-READING seat.\n\nPASS 2 ON #439, 7 of 7 scriptable seats -- the first full scriptable panel of the campaign. THE SIX SOUND VERDICTS CONVERGED ON THE BRIEF\u0027S SUBSTANTIVE QUESTION and NOBODY defended the reload-value design that the pass-1 majority had recommended and the implementing seat built and measured causing a guest divide-by-zero. So the refusal of that majority is VINDICATED by the seats themselves.\n\n*** WHAT ALL SIX MISSED, AND CODEX DID NOT: the latch is never CONSUMED. *** latched[] is cleared only by a non-latch mode write, never by the read, so after one latch the counter returns 0 indefinitely. Handed to the in-flight pitflip round because the consume semantics interact with the LSB/MSB flip-flop that round is fixing. It was my own Q4 in the brief and I did not check it before shipping.",
