                            "note":  "*** commits READ THE LITERAL STRING \u0027PENDING\u0027 UNTIL NOW, AND SECTION K ACCEPTED IT. ***  I wrote it while recording #439 before the commit existed and never came back. A review seat found both halves: the wrong record, and the hole that hid it -- check_witness.py skips only an EMPTY commits field, so \u0027PENDING\u0027 satisfied the witness gate exactly as a real SHA would. Corrected to 020a672.\n\nThe general lesson is the one this project keeps paying: a field nothing validates is a field that drifts. Two rows legitimately carry prose (deadman, pkbrief) for work with no commit, so the fix is not \u0027demand hashes\u0027 -- it is to tell a DELIBERATE non-repo note from a PLACEHOLDER nobody returned to. That check now exists in check_commit_attribution.py.",
