                            "note":  "*** THE DISSENT AGAINST PAIRING WITH pitlatch IS ANSWERABLE ON THE MERITS, AND THE ROUND GAVE THE WEAK REASON. ***  The recorded justification -- \u0027a scope preference is not a measured false pass\u0027 -- is procedural and would retro-justify any pairing. The substantive answer is already in #439\u0027s own detector table: *** the SPLIT proposal IS candidate C2 (\u0027read-arm only\u0027), and C2 FAILS R1. ***  Splitting ships a build where the latch is silently accepted on the read side while the write side still destroys mode_byte -- a known-red row in the round\u0027s own oracle. That is a refutation on the merits, not a scope preference.\n\nUnderlying it: these are not two defects. They are the read side and the write side of ONE COMMAND BEING UNIMPLEMENTED, so prong 3 is satisfied literally.",
