                            "note":  "ADJUDICATION of the nine-seat panel. It read the actual loop and one fact decided three of four decisions: *** `rd(t)` IS A FIXED-DURATION DRAIN. It waits the full `t` EVERY TIME and returns early only on EOF or OSError; it never returns early on `command done`, and the inter-command wait is a hardcoded `rd(0.35)`. *** **D2 -- AND THIS IS THE RULING THAT PREVENTS REAL DAMAGE:** codex\u0027s gate_hygiene fix is THIS ROUND (a gate change, re-measures nothing) **but it must be ENUMERATE-FIRST + RATCHET, not `reject every file lacking an approved predicate`** -- because EVERY CURRENT PROBE IS PROMPTLESS, so a hard reject-all reds the whole battery PERMANENTLY, which is the permanent-red hazard the carrier warns about. Grandfather the existing promptless probes on an explicit list; fail any NEW one. That still gives the closed-world denominator -- you know exactly which files are PTY probes and the set only shrinks -- without retro-failing the archive. *I was about to endorse the reject-all form.* **D3:** the re-measurement cost is REAL and DISQUALIFIES codex\u0027s (1) from any `cheap improvement` framing -- every command\u0027s output accumulates into one `buf` that the row regexes scan whole, so changing when the next command fires changes WHICH WINDOW a line lands in: a count that read 1 could read 2, an `absent` could resolve. **D1:** the conclusion survives, the premise is false, adopt deepseek\u0027s `non-exit predicate` framing WITH A TIGHTENING -- it is False on process exit **or pty error**, so precisely *the child neither exited nor errored the pty during the sampled windows*. **That tightening is not pedantry: it means a red `alive=died` CANNOT TELL A CLEAN EXIT FROM A PTY ERROR** -- the same cause-attribution gap that bit M11\u0027s `absent` firing last round. **D4 -- THE CHEAP FIX EXISTS AND IT IS NOT codex\u0027s (1):** append ONE sentinel command before `quit`, whose unique output matches no scored row\u0027s regex. alive False -\u003e TERMINATED; alive True + sentinel present -\u003e RESPONSIVE; alive True + sentinel absent -\u003e UNRESPONSIVE. **Because it is APPENDED, every existing row\u0027s window and buf content is unchanged, so it RE-MEASURES NOTHING** -- where codex\u0027s (1) re-times every command. Honest limits stated: `unresponsive` still conflates hung with slow (the same ambiguity already on record for the `absent` path, but strictly better than a binary that reads a hang as alive), and it adds one rd() window per session, ~a minute across 39 sessions -- additive and bounded, not a re-measurement. Items (3), (4) and (5) FILED, with (5) -- the rename -- to its own dedicated commit with the diff-every-list check, never bundled, because it touches the hardcoded gate name-list."
