        "state_note":  "  *** THE FILED COUNT OF `FIVE ROWS` IS WRONG: IT IS NINE OF 57, AND SIX OF THE NINE PREDATE #462. Measured 2026-08-24 from the archived log `_scratchpad/kill462/probe_M2.raw`. *** The nine whose got-column is the pure-liveness form (`\u0027survived\u0027 if alive else \u0027died\u0027`, want `survived`) are: rd lo, wr lo, rd hi, rd w16, scan, dma rd, arm survive, nodata live, nodata stale. **So the reframing is NOT confined to the three #462 rows the vacuity-floor carve-out blessed** -- six ordinary read rows in the pre-existing detector assert nothing except that the process did not exit, and under this row\u0027s finding that predicate is TRUE OF A HUNG EMULATOR. *** THE DERIVATION IS RECORDED BECAUSE I GOT IT WRONG TWICE FIRST, in both of the directions the carrier warns about. *** (1) Counting `row()` CALL SITES through `ast` gave `6 of 52` -- but CALL SITES ARE NOT ROWS: the probe emits 58 from 52 literal-label sites because three sites sit inside loops, and the site at :263 has a COMPUTED label, which is exactly why four of the nine (rd lo, wr lo, rd hi, rd w16) cannot be found by grepping for `row(\"name\"`. (2) Anchoring the got-column at offset 14 instead of 15 -- the `%-14s` field is followed by a separator space -- returned `0 of 57`, a clean, confident PHANTOM ABSENCE that would have been read as `no row uses this form`. Both were caught only by carrying the DENOMINATOR: `0 of 57` and `0 of 0` are different claims and only one is evidence.  *** AND THE SECOND HALF OF THIS ROW\u0027S CLAIM MEASURES AS SEVEN, NOT SIX, of 33. *** The filing says `six pty probes have NO prompt detection at all`. Counted 2026-08-24 with one pass -- `grep -l pty.fork *.py` then `xargs grep -L \u0027endswith(\u0027` -- **33 pty-forking probes, 7 with zero occurrences**: drive_guest.py, gdrom_data_probe.py, gdrom_default_probe.py, sh_intprio_probe.py, sh_iprbcd_probe.py, sh_pclock_probe.py, sh_tlbmulti_probe.py. The CLOSED-WORLD mechanism is confirmed by reading `gate_hygiene.sh:97-99`: `py_code()` pipes every file through `xargs -0 grep -h \"endswith(\"`, so a file containing ZERO occurrences contributes to no counter and the ratchet passes. **A probe with no prompt detection is invisible to the ratchet built to catch probes with BAD prompt detection.**  *** AND THE `absent` PATH WENT FROM READING TO MEASUREMENT WITHIN THE HOUR, IN THIS ROUND\u0027S OWN THIRD TABLE. *** The adjudicating seat wrote that printed() returning `absent` would redden the idle rows under a hang, but offered it as `a reading, not a measurement -- no absent-red appears anywhere in the preserved kill map`. Verified: 0 of the 14 table-2 logs contain one. **Table 3\u0027s M11 run contains one.** The comparison, same mutant, two runs: TABLE 2 -- `nodata stale` reads `died`, host TERMINATED, M11 scores 54/57 with three reds. TABLE 3 -- **all NINE liveness rows read `survived`**, so the host never terminated, and M11 scores 56/58 with two reds: `stale says` at `0` against a wanted `1`, and `stale idle` at **`absent`** against `0x0`. *** SO M11\u0027S OBSERVABLE FAILURE IS NOT STABLE ACROSS RUNS -- a NULL-pointer read of 408 bytes faults on one run and does not on another -- AND ON THE RUN WHERE IT DID NOT FAULT, NOT ONE LIVENESS ROW REDDENED. *** Had `stale says` and `stale idle` not existed, M11 would have scored 58/58 and ESCAPED. That is a direct, measured demonstration of why the not-EOF predicate\u0027s blind spot matters, and it arrived inside the very round that was arguing about it. **HONEST LIMIT: `absent` with the process alive is CONSISTENT WITH a hang, and that reading is not yet established** -- it is equally consistent with the session simply outrunning its spin budget. Distinguishing them is exactly what the proposed three-state predicate (terminated / responsive / unresponsive) would do, and it is now the strongest argument for building it. *This also strengthens the case that the DETECTOR is sound while the PREDICATE is not: the value rows caught what the liveness rows could not see.*  *** THE `absent` CENSUS, WITH DENOMINATORS, AND A CONTROL THAT RULES OUT A FLAKY RIG. *** Across every preserved log: table 1 **0 of 10**, table 2 **0 of 14**, table 3 **1 of 4 completed runs** -- so one firing in 28 mutant runs, and it is M11. *** THE CONTROL IS M10, MEASURED IN THE SAME TWO TABLES: its reds are BYTE-IDENTICAL across them -- `arm count2` and `arm enable2` both times, 55/57 then 56/58. *** So the instability is specific to M11\u0027s NULL-source `memory_rw` fault path and is NOT a general property of the rig, the probe, or the host under load. **That distinction is the whole value of the measurement**: without it, `M11\u0027s mode changed` is indistinguishable from `this rig is flaky`, and the second reading would discredit every score in all three tables rather than one cell in one of them.  *** THE STALL DIAGNOSIS WAS CONFIRMED BY INTERVENTION, NOT INFERRED FROM A CONTRAST -- 125 BYTES -\u003e 24,211 BYTES, SAME SEAT, SAME PANEL, SAME EVENING, ONE VARIABLE. *** minimax stalled at 125 bytes on a brief with ZERO inlined code that said `Read gdrom_default_probe.py\u0027s session()/rd()`. The brief was corrected -- `rd()` and the command loop inlined verbatim -- and the same seat was re-fired into the same panel: **24,211 bytes, a 194x difference.** The carrier\u0027s inline-every-fact rule has been stated for months from anecdote; this is the controlled version, and the counterfactual is measured rather than argued. *** AND THE SEAT THAT `STALLED` IMMEDIATELY CORRECTED THIS ROW\u0027S CENTRAL CLAIM. *** This row rests on `rd() returns False ONLY on EOF`. minimax, as soon as it could SEE the code: `this is NOT just EOF -- it could be EIO, EBADF, etc.` The `except OSError` arm catches considerably more than end-of-file, so `alive == False` means `the read raised OSError or returned empty`, not `the process exited`. **That sharpens the row rather than refuting it** -- the hang-blindness stands, since none of those conditions fires for a wedged-but-open pty -- but the premise as written is imprecise and a detector built on the literal wording would mis-describe what it observes. *The seat was never unable to contribute; it was unable to SEE.*  *** THE PANEL CONVERGED ON THE PREMISE, NOT THE CONCLUSION: THREE SEATS INDEPENDENTLY ISOLATED `rd() RETURNS FALSE ONLY ON EOF` AS THE SINGLE LOAD-BEARING AND UNVERIFIED CLAIM -- and one of them showed it is WRONG AS WRITTEN. *** minimax: `rd() claim is wrong` (`except OSError` catches EIO, EBADF). kimi: real `only if` that claim holds. glm: `rests on a single unverified load-bearing premise`. **That is a panel doing the job a panel is for -- not voting on the conclusion, but finding the one sentence everything else hangs from.** deepseek then gave the corrected form its sharpest statement: **`alive` is a NON-EXIT predicate, not a liveness predicate** -- which says what it DOES observe, where the row\u0027s own wording said only what it fails to observe. The conclusion survives (a wedged-but-open pty raises no OSError and returns no EOF, so the hang-blindness stands) but the row must be restated in deepseek\u0027s terms before it is acted on.  *** THE ROUND\u0027S SHAPE IS NOW ADJUDICATED: the cheap fix is a SESSION-TAIL SENTINEL, not a per-command change, and the reason is the corrected premise. *** Because `alive` is a NON-EXIT predicate, the cheapest way to add a liveness reading is ONE EXTRA NON-EXIT CHECK AT THE END -- not re-timing the reads that already work. Appending it leaves every scored row\u0027s window untouched, so it re-measures nothing; codex\u0027s positive-completion detection is the eventual full conversion and carries a fresh matrix. **D1 explains the SHAPE of D4, and D2/D3 keep the expensive forms out of this round.**  *** THE CENSUS NUMERATOR WAS RIGHT AND MY DERIVATION OF IT WAS WRONG IN BOTH HALVES -- corrected 2026-08-25 after a measuring seat re-derived it and I re-checked with `ast`. *** I wrote that the count is `9 of 57` because `three sites sit inside loops, and one site at :263 has a COMPUTED label`. Measured: **EXACTLY TWO** `row()` sites are inside a loop, and **THOSE SAME TWO** carry the computed labels; `:263` is a `put h` format string inside `run()` and emits NO ROW AT ALL. The arithmetic that actually reaches the total is `52 call sites - 2 in-loop + 2 x 4 iterations = 58`. *** AND THE DENOMINATOR WAS STALE: it is 9 of **58**, not 57 -- the shipped probe emits 58 (`GDROM_DEF_RESULT=58/58`). *** So the row said `9 of 57` with a derivation that reaches neither 57 nor 58. **This is the right-conclusion-wrong-reason class the carrier warns gets REUSED**, and it is the second instance in this round: `safe 4`\u0027s warrant claimed `\u0026 1` kills +0x04 when under `\u0026 1` nothing dies. *A reader re-deriving from my sentence does not reach 58, which is the whole test of whether a stated reason is load-bearing or decorative.* **AND THE MORE USEFUL CENSUS IS A DIFFERENT ONE: 13 of 58**, not 9 -- `wantion breaks (`printed()` returns `absent` -\u003e RED), so a hang IS caught loudly by the detector -- it is **MISATTRIBUTED**, reading as value failures rather than as a hung session. Strictly better than blind, and the cost is DIAGNOSIS, not detection: a hang regression reddens the battery but the signature points at values. *** AND THE TWO SUPPOSEDLY-BLIND ROWS ARE IN DIFFERENT STATES, which the verify-across-all-tables caveat caught before the record could call both `genuinely blind`: *** `accept8` has NO recorded kill anywhere -- genuinely unproven coverage. `dma accept` **HAS a measured kill on record** -- `m_deldma18`, 31/32, reddening that row alone -- but it is a **#461** mutant, so it is absent from all three #462 tables (verified: 0 red across 40 mutant runs) **and its per-row log is in the `killartifacts` gap**, making it verifiable from PROSE ONLY. *That is this session\u0027s own archive defect blocking the verification of a claim, in the round that filed it and wrote the durability rule against it.* FILED as coverage debt, not owed: a row with no kill is UNPROVEN coverage, not a demonstrated false pass, so the stopping rule files it.  *** PARTIAL SHIP at `abf665c`, and the row STAYS OPEN: that commit corrected the probe\u0027s own CONTRACT (a wrong record about what `alive` observes) but did NOT fix the predicate. *** The distinction matters for anyone reading the row later: what shipped is the honest description -- `alive` means no EOF and no OSError were seen inside the sampled windows, it is True for a hung, a frozen AND an already-killed process, and a red `alive == died` cannot tell a clean exit from a pty error. What is still OWED is the fix: the session-tail sentinel giving three states (terminated / responsive / unresponsive), which re-measures nothing because it is APPENDED. *A row that ships a corrected record and keeps its defect open is the normal case, not an anomaly -- and naming the commit is what stops the correction from later being mistaken for the fix.*",
        "note":  "  *** CITATIONS RE-DERIVED 2026-08-31 AND BOTH LOOK STALE. ***  This row cites `gate_hygiene.sh:97-98`; today those are comment lines about harness code being left in scope, not about prompt detection.  The subject -- promptless pty probes -- is discussed at the comment *\"TEN pty-forking promptless probes sat\"*, and note the COUNT there is TEN while this row\u0027s title says SIX.  **Two possibilities and I did not resolve them: either the row is scoped to a subset, or one of the two counts has drifted.**  Recorded as an open question rather than guessed, because picking one would be exactly the kind of confident reconciliation the wrong-tree and stale-citation rules both warn against.  **DURABLE ANCHOR: `grep -n \u0027promptless probes\u0027 regress/gate_hygiene.sh`.**  *ANCHOR CAVEAT, stated rather than glossed: `\u0027promptless probes\u0027` matches TWICE in `gate_hygiene.sh`, and the citation-form rule asks for VERIFIED-UNIQUE anchors.  Two hits still locate the discussion and both are in the same comment block, so it is usable -- but it is not unique, and saying so is the difference between an anchor that was checked and one that was asserted.  The other two anchors minted today match exactly once.*  *** THE HYGIENE GATE WILL GO RED ON THE NEXT WEEKLY BATTERY, AND IT WILL BE RIGHT. got=15 want=11. ***  Four pty-forking probes have no prompt detection and are not in `GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS`:  `gdrom_cond_probe.py`, **`sgi_re_width_probe.py`**, `wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py`, `wdc_altoffset_probe.py`.  *** ONE OF THEM IS #497\u0027s DETECTOR, SHIPPED BY THIS SESSION TODAY, AND THAT IS RECORDED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT FOR THE BATTERY TO REPORT AS A SURPRISE. ***  **They are genuinely promptless, not misclassified -- checked, because the gate\u0027s own comment warns that `grep -L \u0027endswith(\u0027` cannot see REGEX readiness and would produce false positives.**  All four carry `re.search`/`re.match`, so the warning applies; but in `sgi_re_width_probe.py` the regex PARSES a register value (`print\\s+%s\\s*\\n\\s*(0x...)`) while the wait is `while time.time() \u003c end` around `select.select` -- a TIME-BASED wait with no prompt predicate.  That is this row\u0027s defect exactly.  **THE COUNT IN THIS ROW\u0027S TITLE (SIX) IS STALE, AND SO IS THE TEN IN THE GATE\u0027S COMMENT -- AND THEY WERE NEVER THE SAME POPULATION.**  The gate comment\u0027s TEN counts promptless probes *under `artifacts/`*, which the denominator deliberately excludes; today that population is **20**.  The live promptless count is 15.  So the two numbers differ because they always counted different sets, and both have since drifted.  *The gate\u0027s own comment anticipates precisely this: \"Re-derive rather than quote; if the two ever differ, that difference is the finding.\"*  *** MY FIRST DISPOSITION HERE SAID \"DO NOT GRANDFATHER THE FOUR\" AND THE GATE REFUTES IT IN CAPITALS: \"ADDING THEM TO THE GRANDFATHERED SET IS NOT A BYPASS, AND THE DISTINCTION IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE ROW.  This list is not `probes we forgive`; it is `promptless probes we KNOW about`, and the check\u0027s job is to NAME any that appear unnoticed.\"  I read \"the reason written down rather than the count quietly raised\" as forbidding the raise; it forbids the QUIET raise. ***  A red row here is the mechanism working: four probes really do lack readiness, and one arrived today.  The repair is to give them a prompt predicate, which is a round of its own and not a rider on this one.  Letting the battery red honestly costs one red row; suppressing it costs the only check that notices promptless probes at all.  *** AND THERE WAS A SECOND RED ROW I HAD NOT SEEN: `EXPECT_PTY_PROBES=37` against a measured denominator of 41.  Both pins short by exactly four -- the same four -- which is the arithmetic that makes this ONE event rather than two. ***  **A failed gate is a failed battery, and the next one was ~17 hours out.**  Both pins raised WITH PER-MEMBER REASONS, and the four do not share one: `wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py` and `wdc_altoffset_probe.py` are breakpoint-driven -- promptless for exactly the reason the existing members are, and the first says so in its own comment -- while `gdrom_cond_probe.py` and `sgi_re_width_probe.py` are TIME-BASED DRAINS with no prompt predicate at all, which is a WEAKER reason and is recorded as such rather than folded in.  *The second group is this row\u0027s live defect; listing them does not forgive them, it makes them tracked instead of invisible.*  **CONTROLLED BOTH WAYS before commit:** with the four added both rows are GREEN (41/41, 15/15); dropping any ONE reds the promptless row at got=15 want=14, so the check still fires rather than having been switched off.  *And `sgi_re_width_probe.py` was added by #497 -- this session -- so the pin was raised by the round that broke it.  Disclosed in the gate comment rather than absorbed.*  *TITLE CORRECTED 2026-08-31.  It read \"six pty probes have NO prompt detection at all\"; re-derived with the gate\u0027s OWN computation the live count is **15** -- 11 grandfathered plus 4 that had arrived since the pin was set.  The old figure named neither its unit nor its method and could not be checked, which is exactly the class the counts rule exists for.  The gate comment\u0027s competing \"TEN\" was never the same population: it counts promptless probes under `artifar:regress/artifacts/gdromwarnbits/bound_assert_controls.sh -- the COMPILE-TIME bound assert gdrom_w_fits_its_carriers, with a five-way control run preserved beside it. *** THIS FIELD READ `harness:` AND WAS MIS-FILED; corrected 2026-08-28 on the assess panel, where the fable5 seat named it. *** `harness:` is admitted only when the round\u0027s SUBJECT is the test apparatus, and this round\u0027s subject is PRODUCT code. The controls are two-sided on purpose: CLEAN on the shipped source and at nine bits over uint32_t, ERROR at nine over uint8_t, at 33 over uint32_t, and at 40 over uint64_t -- so the guard is demonstrably not a check that cannot fail. The superseded offline mask_equivalence_check.c remains as PROVENANCE only: two seats measured that it duplicates the definitions rather than including them, so it is an AUDIT of one moment and cannot see product drift. RUNG-3 ATTEMPT, per the 2026-08-27 lifecycle ruling: not applicable by construction -- the defect is a COMPILE-TIME representation bound, latent at six bits and unreachable by any guest access on HEAD.",
        "title":  "gdromwarnbits  six of eight warn bits are used and they are hand-assigned hex masks; the ninth overflows a uint8_t SILENTLY and floods",
        "entries":  [
                        {
                            "seat":  "fable5",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "�o"",
                            "date":  "2026-08-23",
                            "note":  "Raised by the main loop while writing #462\u0027s pass-2 brief, then checked against the tree. `d-\u003ewarned` is a uint8_t and GDROM_W_LEN/NODATA/NOTWAIT/OVERREAD/DMANODATA/DMAARM are hand-assigned 0x01..0x20 -- SIX of eight, and #462 is what took it from four to six. *** THE FAILURE MODE AT NINE IS SILENT, WHICH IS WHY IT IS WORTH FILING RATHER THAN NOTING. *** `warned |= (1u \u003c\u003c 8)` truncates to 0 in a uint8_t, so the latch never sets, `!(warned \u0026 BIT)` stays true forever, and the diagnostic FLOODS -- the exact behaviour every one of these latches exists to prevent, arriving with no compile error and no runtime complaint. A duplicate hand-assigned mask fails the same way for a different reason: two sites share one bit and the second is silenced by the first. *** THE ZERO-COST STRUCTURAL FIX HAS IN-TREE PRECEDENT AND THE CARRIER RECORDS IT. *** dev_sh4.c:124-263 converted its SH4_VAL_* defines to a C99 enum ending in SH4_VAL_NCLASS, \u0027correct by construction instead of by maintenance\u0027. The shapes differ -- those are ARRAY INDICES, these are BIT MASKS -- so the analogue is an enum of bit POSITIONS ending in GDROM_W_NBITS, with each mask defined as `1u \u003c\u003c GDROM_W_x_B`. Duplicates become impossible, and NBITS gives a checkable bound against the width of `warned`. *** NOT FIXED NOW, AND FILED WITH A PRE-SET TRIGGER, WHICH IS HOW THE SH4 ONE GOT DONE ON TIME. *** That conversion carried the trigger \u0027when a tenth class arrives\u0027; SH4_VAL_SCICMD was the tenth and the work happened. #462\u0027s semantic class is de-fatalising the DMA pair -- converting the latch representation is a different change, and the stopping rule reserves in-round work for a measured false pass or a wrong record. THE TRIGGER HERE: **the seventh warn bit**. At seven, widen `warned` and convert to the enum form in the same edit; there is no reason to wait for the overflow."
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "opus5",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-27",
                            "grade":  "CONFIRMED",
                            "ev":  "src/devices/dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c + a compiled mask-equivalence check",
                            "note":  "*** THE PRE-SET TRIGGER FIRED EXACTLY AS WRITTEN, AND THAT IS THE FINDING WORTH KEEPING\nAS MUCH AS THE CONVERSION. ***  It was set as \u0027at the SEVENTH bit\u0027.  `gdromexitsix` Round\n1 adds THREE latches to the six in use, so the NINTH would be `1u \u003c\u003c 8` -- truncating to\nzero in a uint8_t, never setting, and letting the diagnostic it guards FLOOD, with no\ncompile error and no runtime complaint.\n\nTWO SEATS REACHED IT INDEPENDENTLY on that round\u0027s pass 1: the adjudicator named it as an\nobligation the brief had missed entirely, and agy called it a critical implementation\nblocker.  Neither was told about the trigger; both derived the budget from the code.\n\nCONVERSION: six `#define`d masks -\u003e an enum of bit POSITIONS ending in GDROM_W_NBITS, with\neach mask `(1u \u003c\u003c ..._B)`, and `warned` widened uint8_t -\u003e uint32_t.  GDROM_W_NBITS is now\ncorrect BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by maintenance, and a duplicate mask is impossible to\\nits value-class keys on its own pre-set trigger (\u0027when a tenth class arrives\u0027), and the\ncarrier records that one as discharged.  A trigger set in advance, fired by an unrelated\nround, and discharged without a fresh design argument is the cheapest thing in this\nproject -- and it only worked because the condition was written down as a CONDITION rather\nthan as a note saying \u0027watch out for this\u0027.*"
                        },
                        {
                            "seait: (HELD-AWAITING-SEAT fable5 -- marker defanged so this QUOTE of it does not re-arm gen_codex_wall.py)  QUESTION: **does discharging a PRE-SET TRIGGER need a full\npanel?**\n\nThe trigger in `dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c` was written in advance -- \u0027at the   This round detected the condition and executed it;\nbehaviour-preservation is MEASURED (all six masks bit-identical, by a compiled check), not\nargued.\n\nI closed the row on two seats and the gate refused.  It was right to.  But the underlying\nquestion is real: nine seats on a decided, mechanical, measured-equivalent refactor may be\nthe wrong use of the roster -- or the rule may be exactly right, because \u0027it was decided in\nadvance\u0027 is what every unreviewed change says about itself.\n\nMY "
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "opus5",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "THE SEAT THAT FOUND WHAT NO OTHER SEAT DID, AND IT IS INSIDE THIS FILE\u0027S OWN TRANSLATION UNIT. *** dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c:46 INCLUDES thirdparty/dreamcast_sysasicvar.h, AND EVERY SYSASIC_TRIGGER_EVENT() CALL EXPANDS SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK -- A C99 COMPILE-TIME BOUND ASSERT. FOUR of them compile on every build, two hundred lines below a comment saying the technique is unavailable to this tree. *** Census of the idiom, multi-line aware (it flagged that its own first single-line grep undercounted): FOUR sites -- cpu_mips.c x2 (#388), memory_rw.c (#430), sysasicvar.h (#468/#469, bitfield form). Chronology airtight: #430 ships the idiom 08-15; gdrom\u0027s C99 rationale written 08-23; #468 REFUTES that rationale by measurement 08-26; this code ships 08-27. THREE FURTHER L4s NOBODY ELSE RAISED, all corrected this round: the trigger comment SURVIVED ITS OWN DISCHARGE verbatim and in the PRESENT TENSE (still saying \u0027SIX OF EIGHT BITS\u0027 when it is six of 32, and \u0027truncates to 0 in a uint8_t\u0027 when the field is uint32_t); the C99 rationale at the GDROM_UNIMPL_FIRST comment; and \u0027THE PRE-SET TRIGGER ABOVE HAS FIRED\u0027 pointing the wrong DIRECTION (the trigger is below). MEASURED: GDROM_W_NBITS had ZERO consumers -- it sized nothing, bounded nothing, and DELETING it compiled clean -- so \u0027correct BY CONSTRUCTION\u0027 rested on a decorative symbol, and the shipped assert is its FIRST CONSUMER, which makes it L4 repair rather than accretion. 16-variant kill table with four legal configurations as negative controls: the brief\u0027s own proposed `GDROM_W_NBITS \u003c= 32` ESCAPES the 9-bits-over-uint8_t defect -- MEASURED VACUOUS against floor clauses (b)/(d). CONCEDED the shipped form\u0027s clause 2 as a real hole in its own proposal (its one-clause form accepts 40 positions over a uint64_t field, where `1u \u003c\u003c 40` is UB). Verified \u0027emits no object code\u0027 with the filename held constant: the object differs in exactly TWO bytes, both __LINE__ immediates displaced +50 by the comment block. Found the dev_sh4.c ASYMMETRY: SH4_VAL_NCLASS SIZES an array and bounds a runtime check, so ITS by-construction claim is true unaided, while GDROM_W_NBITS\u0027s was not -- the precedent transfers on shape but NOT on the property it was cited for. Population CONFIRMED at twelve and the truncation hunt NEGATIVE: no cast, no %hh anywhere in src/, the struct never escapes the file, and the tree has no save-state machinery at all. Disclosed its own apparatus failure: two of its scripts raced on one scratch directory and one deleted the other\u0027s inputs; it re-ran isolated and stands behind only the clean table.",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715 (Agent seat, leaves no file in the panel dir)"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "fable5",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "ADJUDICATOR HAT. RATIFIES THE GATE\u0027S REFUSAL, and states the clean rule: *** THE UNIT OF PANEL COVERAGE IS THE COMMIT, NOT THE DECISION. *** A discharge riding inside an already-panelled round is covered; one shipping as its OWN commit owes its own stage. That resolves the dev_sh4.c readback WITHOUT retro-condemning it -- the SH4_VAL conversion shipped inside panelled round #451, so it stands and the carrier\u0027s DISCHARGED record is undisturbed. Refuted the brief\u0027s central A4 premise: the sysasicvar.h citation is INVERTED -- the block records #466\u0027s comment-only rationale being REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT on its pass 2, and the range IS now enforced at compile time; the brief cited the header of the very block that refutes it. Ruled A4(a) NOT an L4 (the sentence\u0027s subject is the COUNT, which is by-construction correct, and the same comment block already says \u0027not asserted here\u0027), while tempering the \u0027a duplicate is impossible to write\u0027 clause -- which is the half the round corrected. Ruled A4(c) LICENSED: a transferred warrant from memory_rw.c\u0027s own licence sentence (\u0027a static assertion costs nothing and covers the build the test cannot reach\u0027), plus a measured kill table, and NOT the dead-guard shape, because a negative-array typedef emits no object code and cannot defeat a row. Proposed the field-bound predicate that replaced the brief\u0027s wrong one. Flagged the row\u0027s witness field as mis-filed under the taxonomy. Ran its own compile measurements (t1-t6).",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715 (Agent seat, leaves no file in the panel dir)"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "codex",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "VERDICT: NO IN PRINCIPLE -- a pre-set trigger avoids a seconFECT IN THE VERIFICATION ARTIFACT AND STATED IT MOST SHARPLY: mask_equivalence_check.c DUPLICATES the definitions rather than including them, so adding bits to the PRODUCT leaves the artifact\u0027s private GDROM_W_NBITS equal to six forever -- product drift leaves the offline check COMPLETELY GREEN and apparently healthy. *** So the brief\u0027s own \u0027LOUD only if someone runs the offline check\u0027 premise is FALSE, and the artifact is an AUDIT rather than a CHECK. Ruled A4(a) an L4 and supplied the precise replacement wording. PROPOSED THE TWO-CLAUSE ASSERT THAT SHIPPED, with the reason the other seats\u0027 forms lacked: the masks shift `1u`, so storage width alone does not prove the SHIFT OPERAND wide enough on every C99 target. Confirmed the twelpad/panel_20260828_105715"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "grok",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "VERDICT: DO NOT WAIVE THE NINE-SEAT PANEL. *** THE DECISIVE ARGUMENT OF THE STAGE, AND IT IS INSTITUTIONAL RATHER THAN TECHNICAL: \u0027THE RULE IS ALREADY A GATE, NOT A TASTE.\u0027 *** tools/pipeline/cFAILS that test. Enumerated the choices the trigger did not fix: the width; a disconnected copy as the witness; leaving the old present-tense trigger comment standing; and \u0027by construction\u0027 being read to cover the bound. Independently caught thatT.md was stale against HEAD at the moment it read -- true then, and rewritten the same morning.",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715"
                        },
                        {
                            "sanest statement of the circularity: \u0027the no-design-choices claim is self-serving and circular -- the party executing the discharge is the same party claiming no design choices were made.\u0027 Named three unreviewed choices in the commit, and ONE THAT NO OTHER SEAT NAMED: *** selecting uint32_t rather than a DYNAMICALLY BOUNDED BITSET ARRAY, citing this same struct\u0027s own unimpl_reported[GDROM_NDIR][GDROM_BITWORDS(GDROM_NKEYS)] as the in-file precedent for the alternative shape. *** That is an OPTION-SET COMPLETENESS finding -- a member nobody had put in the option set -- and it is exactly the class the carrier\u0027s three-membered-option-set rule exists to surface. Also independently identified the sysasicvar.h compile-time precedent and that the C99 premise was mistaken, and called the verification artifact an isolated offline mock rather than an integrated regression check.",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "deepseek",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "PACKET-FED. VERDICT: the widening and mask conversion ARE discharged by the trigger and the equivalence check, so no full panel for THAT delta -- but the \u0027by construction\u0027 overclaim and the absence of a bound assertion are new design choices the trigger did not fix, so a panel is required to rule on A4(a)-(c) before the row can close. HONEST ABOUT ITS LIMITS, which is the form this project asks of a packet-fed seat: it marked A1c NOT CHECKABLE from the packet and named the exact settling fact (a full grep of GDROM_W_ and warned, plus inspection of any save-state code). Its position differs from the file-reading seats in SCOPE rather than in substance -- it too concludes the row cannot close on the evidence as given.",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "minimax",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "PACKET-FED. VERDICT: targeted scrutiny rather than a full nine-seat panel; the equivalence check has a real gap (FIELD WIDTH UNTESTED); the \u0027by construction\u0027 comment is an overclaim; and it LEANS AGAINST the guard under the addition licence. *** ITS REFRAME IS THE SHARPEST SENTENCE ANY PACKET-FED SEAT PRODUCED: \u0027the honest question is not whether the trigger fixed every design choice, but whether the DISCHARGE introduced a defect the trigger did not foreclose\u0027 -- and it then lists them as IMPLEMENTATION defects rather than design choices, noting that a trigger which fixes design does not immunise the discharge against an incorrect edit. *** It reached the field-width gap in the checker from the packet alone. ITS A4(c) LEAN AGAINST THE GUARD IS THE STAGE\u0027S ONLY OPPOSING VOTE ON THAT POINT AND IS RECORDED AS SUCH, not folded into a majority: it was outweighed by two independent measured kill tables and a transferred in-tree warrant, not by a count of seats.",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "glm",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "PACKET-FED. *** ITS VERDICT LINE IS A DEFECT IN MY OWN BRIEF AND IT LED WITH IT: \u0027the brief\u0027s inlined measurement contains a verbatim output that its own inlined source code cannot produce.\u0027 *** Correct, and mine: I condensed three printf lines when inlining mask_equivalence_check.c while quoting its .out VERBATIM, so the source shown could not have produced the output shown. codex, fable5 and opus5 each found the same thing independently; glm is the seat that made it the HEADLINE, and it is right that it undermines the \u0027measured behaviour-preserving\u0027 premise AS PRESENTED -- the artifacts on disk are self-consistent with each other, the packet was not. Marked A1c and the C99-precedent premise uncheckable from the packet and named the settling searches. Conditional rather than absolute on the hold question: no full panel IF the measurement holds, and it judged that it did not.",
                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260828_105715"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "kimi",
                            "phase":  "assess",
                            "d":  "OK",
                            "date":  "2026-08-28",
                            "note":  "PACKET-FED, via the kimi-k3:cloud SUBSTITUTE transport -- the kimi CLI is 403-walled on its billing cycle and its 350-byte error file is NOT a seat answer. Recorded by TRANSPORT, per the sixth seat-failure class. VERDICT: a pre-set trigger discharges without a nine-seat panel, but THIS ROW MUST NOT CLOSE on the evidence given. *** It derived the correct invariant FROM THE PACKET ALONE -- \u0027the check stays green because it never references the field), agreeing with opus5 and codex who measured it. And it disposed of the brief\u0027s own A3 worry cleanly: mask-VALUE equivalence is provable by hand arithmetic from the packet, so \u0027compiled                   "outcome_note":  "Every element I could check was correct: assess IS 9/9, 84765ec DID ship 122 lines of product code under this row while `commits` named only 84f6682, and my HELD marker was added to an already-complete stage.",
       trigger discharge needs a panel only if it makes a choice the\ntrigger did not already fix\u0027 -- IS REJECTED AS A LICENCE, and rejected for the reason I\nmyself flagged, now measured rather than rhetorical: AN AUTHOR CANNOT ENUMERATE THE\nCHOICES THEY Dd nothing, and DELETING it compiled clean\u0027.\n**So the discharge\u0027s central \u0027correct BY CONSTRUCTION\u0027 claim rested on a decorative\nsymbol**, and was false until the panel\u0027s own finding made NBITS load-bearing.\n\nAND THE PRECEDENT I TRANSFERRED WAS TRANSFERRED ON SHAPE, NOT ON PROPERTY:\n`SH4_VAL_NCLASS` sizes an array and bounds a runtime check, so its by-construction claim\nis true unaided; `GDROM_W_NBITS` was not.  Same conversion, and the property it was cited\nfor was present in one case and absent in the other.  *The trigger\u0027s author could not\nhave known they were making that choice -- which is the whole argument.*\n\nTHE RULE, in applicable form:\n  A pre-set trigger buys exactly ONE thing: the DESIGN debate.  When it fires, the round\n  executes the settled form without re-opening pass-1 design, and the brief cites the\n  trigger VERBATIM as a settled premise.  **It buys nothing at REVIEW**: the executed diff\n  is panelled like any diff -- riding in the firing round\u0027s pass 2, or on its own full\n  stage whose brief inlines the whole diff -- and the row closes only on full stages.\n  The discharge brief NAMES the trigger verbatim and LISTS every delta between the\n  trigger\u0027s text and the executed diff, so seats review the choices actually made instead\n  of re-litigating the settled form.\n\nTHE BOUND, so the panel requirement cannot un-make triggers: a discharge-panel dissent\nagainst the settled FORM itself (enum-ness, count suffix, mask shape) is a LATE DESIGN\nDISSENT -- it files under the late-dissent rule\u0027s disposition 3 and does NOT block the\ndischarge.  The panel\u0027s jurisdiction is the execution and its unfixed choices.\n\n**THE GATE\u0027S FOUR REFUSALS WERE CORRECT EVERY TIME**, which is worth -ARMS `gen_codex_wall.py` AND WOULD HAVE COUNTED THIS COMPLETED 9/9 STAGE AS HELD. ***  Defanged in place.  The rule is already written down -- \u0027before quoting any string a tool matches on, ask what that tool will do with your copy of it\u0027 -- and I broke it inside an entry recording an adjudication about records discipline."
                        }
                    ],
        "state_note":  "  *** RECLASSIFIED 2026-08-24 (fable5 queue ranking): NOT A ROUND -- an IN-ROUND PREREQUISITE of `gdromcondlies`, and folded into that round\u0027s cost. *** The trigger is arithmetic and already known: 6 warn bits are used and `gdromcondlies` adds 3, so 9 latches exceed a `uint8_t` and the enum conversion must happen inside that round rather than being y for e in [0,95]: high events decode to DROPPED fourth-word offsets OR to LEGAL mask-register cases that clobber guest state, and no r-guard can see the second kind",
        "state":  "open",
        "commits":  "9ca9cca",
        "closure":  {
                        "by":  "",
                        "badge":  "",
                        "note":  ""
                    },
        "hold":  "",
        "witness":  "none -- LATENT, and provably so: the highest defined event is 67 \u003c 96",
        "state_note":  "*** #466\u0027s PASS 2 OVERTURNED THE ADJUDICATION THAT SHIPPED IT. TWO SEATS INDEPENDENTLY REFUTED THE \u0027NO BUILD-TIME CHECK IS POSSIBLE\u0027 RULING, AND ONE OF THEM BUILT ALL FOUR VARIANTS. #468 ships the guard. ***\n\nThe adjudicator rejected a compile-time check on SHAPE: *an assert can only reference NAMED terms, so a future `#define SYSASIC_EVENT_FOO 96` adds a name it does not mention and compiles clean.* **That is true of a STANDALONE assert and false of a check INSIDE THE MACRO**, which fires at the RAISE and therefore cannot be bypassed by adding a name.\n\nMEASURED by the opus5 seat, four variants under the real build compiler:\n\n    V0 shipped macro           feared edit compiles CLEAN   \u003c- the defect\n    V1 standalone assert       CLEAN   \u003c- adjudicator\u0027s objection CONFIRMED\n    V2 check inside the macro  ERROR: negative array size\n    V3 bitfield width          ERROR: negative width in bit-field\n\n**V3 is preferred over V2 and the reason is measured:*T at an r==3 offset no detector row touches\n\n**THE THIRD IS DIFFERENT IN KIND and should not be folded with the other two:** it is a DETECTOR-COVERAGE question, not a product invariant. `kill far` (+0xfc) was added to defeat a GROUP-NARROWING mutant and  header licence question stands.\n\n*** SCOPED 2026-08-26 WITHOUT A RUN -- the row is read-only by construction, and the scoping found a CONSTRAINT that changes the fix\u0027s cost. ***\n\n**THE FIX SITE IS A VENDORED THIRDPARTY HEADER.** The macro is at `src/include/thirdparty/dreamcast_sysasicvar.h`, which carries BOTH a GXemul `$Id$` and an upstream **`$NetBSD: sysasicvar.h,v 1.5`** line. **MEASURED: `git log --all -- \u0027src/include/thirdparty/*\u0027` returns TWO commits -- the 0.7.0 import, and the single ~119-correction hardening commit.** So this fork has edited thirdparty exactly ONCE.\n\n*The precedent is not absent, and it cuts both ways: the header\u0027s own banner says it was \"Extended with useful macros and also some more event definitions described in KOS comments\", so GXemul UPSTREAM already extends this vendored file. Editing it is precedented -- it is just rare, and rarity is the cost.*\n\n**WHY THAT MATTERS RATHER THAN BEING TRIVIA:** the row\u0027s whole reason for existing separately is that *the edit which reaches this defect adds a `#define` to a header, with no device-file change at all* -- so a structural-invariant comment in `dev_dreamcast_asic.c` cannot govern it. **The only place a guard can sit is the same rarely-touched header**, which means the fix\u0027s licence question is sharper than for an in-file addition.\n\n**THE CANDIDATE FIX, stated so it can be adjudicated rather than argued:** a compile-time assertion beside the macro, so that adding an event `\u003e= 96` fails the BUILD rather than silently routing to relative `0x0c` and indexing three-element arrays at 3. It is self-verifying by construction -- a negative control is one test `#define` -- and it costs nothing at runtime.\n\n**BUT IT IS AN ADDITION TO PRODUCT CODE, so the ADDITION LICENCE governs: a MEASURED DELTA or a TRANSFERRED WARRANT, never \u0027it cannot hurt\u0027.** The delta cannot be measured without a build, and the machine is reserved (owner directive 2026-08-26: hold off on anything needing an idle macan me.\n\n*** WHAT IS NOT IN DOUBT AND NEEDED NO RUN: the arithmetic. *** `(e)\u003e\u003e5 == 3` for every `e \u003e= 96`; the highest defined event is 67; therefore latent today, and reachable by a one-line header addition by anyone adding a high event n96 gives `(e)\u003e\u003e5 == 3` and a relative offset of 0x0c -- which `dev_dreamcast_asic.c`\u0027s `r = (relative_addr / 4) \u0026 3` maps to index 3 of three-element arrays. **LATENT AND PROVABLY SO: the highest defined event is 67 (MATOUTOFMEM), and both the 67 and the 96 threshold were confirmed from source by two seats.** *** WHY IT IS A SEPARATE ROW RATHER THAN PART OF asicbadaddr: THE EDIT THAT REACHES IT ADDS A #define TO A HEADER, WITH NO CHANGE TO THE DEVICE FILE AT ALL -- so the structural-invariant comment asicbadaddr plans to leave in `dev_dreamcast_asic.c` CANNOT GOVERN IT. *** Post-fix the failure mode also changes rather than disappearing: an event \u003e= 96 would write to 0x0c, fall to `default:`, and the pending bit would be SILENTLY LOSefine block IN THE HEADER. **FILED RATHER THAN SHIPPED THIS ROUND, and the reason is the file class:** the header lives under `src/include/thirdparty/`, which this fork HAS edited (the 8dd86b5 hardening commit) but where NO file carries the `/* #NNN: */ ` t_asic.c` and name this header path as a separate latent item, rather than claiming the invariant is fully protected. ***  *** CORRECTED 2026-08-25 BY THE #463 RECORDS AUDIT (`_scratchpad/panel_20260825_024101_audit`, grok seat), and the correction makes this row STRONGER. *** Every earlier statement of this row said the macro reaches `0x0c` for \"any event \u003e= 96\". **That is false**: `SYSASIC_EVENT_TO_ADDR(e) = SYSASIC_BASE + 4*((e)\u003e\u003e5)` (`dreamcast_sysasicvar.h:74`) sends `e` in `[128,159]` to `+0x10`, which is r = 0 and perfectly legal. The true predicate is `(e\u003e\u003e5) \u0026 3 == 3` -- `[96,127]` -\u003e `+0x0c`, `[224,255]` -\u003e `+0x1c`, `[352,383]` -\u003e `+0x2c`, `[480,511]` -\u003e `+0x3c`. So the violator is not a single range above a threshold but a REPEATING FAMILY that lands on the fourth word of every 16-byte group -- the same structural shape as `asicbadaddr` itself, one level up in the header. Verified by enumerating `4*(e\u003e\u003e5)` over `e\u003e\u003e5` in `[0,15]`. The LATENCY argument is unchanged and still holds: max over all 21 `SYSASIC_EVENT_*` defines is 67 (`:72`), and `67\u003e\u003e5 == 2` lands at `+0x08`.\n\n*** CLOSURE PROPOSED, NOT MADE.  Verified by me against the source; held for the 2026-09-09\nadjudication because a row closed on one seat\u0027s reading plus my own agreement is exactly the\nself-review the conflict-of-interest badge exists to disclose. ***\n**codex (rating pass, 2026-09-07): `low -- the named domain hazard is ALREADY GUARDED`.**  *\"the\nheader now embeds `((e) \u003e= 0 \u0026\u0026 (e) \u003c 96) ? 1 : -1` in `SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK(e)`, which\n`SYSASIC_EVENT_TO_ADDR(e)` invokes.\"*\n\n**VERIFIED BY READING:** `dreamcast_sysasicvar.h:135` defines `SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK` and `:140`\nis `(SYSASIC_BASE + 4*((e)\u003e\u003e5) + SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK(e))` -- the guard is inside the macro, so an\nout-of-domain event cannot produce an address at all.  Added by `#467`/`#468` (`29b450c`), whose\ntitle says *\"the ASIC domain is now ENFORCED\"*.\n\n**The row\u0027s own witness text is now STALE**: it reads *\"LATENT, and provably so: the highest defined\nevent is 67 \u003c 96\"*, which was the pre-fix warrant for it being latent.  The current warrant is\nstronger and different -- the macro rejects the domain structurally -- and that is what the closure\nshould record."
    },
