        "witness":  "measured -- _scratchpad/panel_20260825_024101_audit/consistency_deepseek-v4-pro_cloud.txt",
        "state_note":  "*** TWO MORE INSTANCES 2026-08-26, BACK TO BACK, AND THEY CARRY A CORRELATION THIS ROW DID NOT HAVE: THE BURN TRACKS BRIEF COMPLEXITY, NOT THE SEAT. ***\n\n    panel_20260826_090604    4,032 b   normal answer\n    panel_20260826_190055    2,845 b   normal answer\n    panel_20260826_222557  142,525 b   BURNED  done_reason=length  eval_counns spanning two rounds. The two clean runs were simpler briefs to the same seat, same transport, same day.\n\n*** THAT REFRAMES THE CLASS. *** The row recorded it as a SEAT property -- something to detect and work around. Today\u0027s evidence says it is at least partly a BRIEF property, which is actionable in a way a seat outage is not: **I can shorten the brief.** That matches the carrier\u0027s oldest lesson about packet-fed seats -- their behaviour is governed by the brief, and this project once spent DAYS misdiagnosing a brief defect as a seat outage.\n\n**AND THE SECOND BURN SHOWS WHAT IS BEING LOST, which the first instance could not.** Its output ends mid-sentence: *\u0027So verdict likely NOT RATIFY due to #467. But maybe the question is from a panel\u0027* -- **it had REACHED a verdict and was second-guessing itself when the budget ran out.** That is a substantive dissent destroyed by a token limit, not a seat with nothing to say. On that same panel the other dissenting seat found a LIVE DEFECT, so a lost dissent here is not hypothetical cost.\n\n**DETECTION IS ALREADY SOLVED AND SHOULD NOT BE RE-ARGUED:** `seat_verdicts.py` reports these as `SEAT DOWN -- spent its whole budget on hidden reasoning (length, N tokens)`, by reading `done_reason` rather than size. Both of today\u0027s burns were caught and named correctly.\n\n**WHAT IS STILL OWED is the MITIGATION, and it is now cheap to state:** keep a packet-fed brief to ONE question with the facts inlined, rather than a multi-part audit. Splitting a complex brief across two firings costs one extra invocation and preserves the answer.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-25 on the #463 consistency audit. `deepseek-v4-pro:cloud` returned **`\"response\": \"\"` -- completely empty -- inside a 265,845-byte JSON object whose `thinking` field is 260,678 bytes, with `done_reason: \u0027length\u0027` and `eval_count: 65536`. It spent its ENTIRE output budget on hidden reasoning and never emitted an answer. *** IT IS DISTINCT FROM ALL FOUR RECORDED CLASSES. *** Not a WALL (no quota text, no 403/429). Not the ECHO-ONLY shape (it echoes nothing). Not a REFUSED CONNECTION (the daemon served it fine, for 267 seconds). Not the shared-transport outage (the other three cloud seats answered normally in the same firing). *** AND IT DEFEATSlesson in a new variant, where the bulk is not an echoed brief but the model\u0027s own reasoning. **It was diagnosable only by accident**: `panel_ollama.py` does `body = resp.get(\u0027response\u0027) or json.dumps(resp)`, so an empty response falls back  cheap: the seat check must parse any Ollama output that starts with `{`, and report SEAT DOWN when `response` is empty -- naming `done_reason` and `eval_count`, because `length` says \u0027budget exhausted\u0027 while `stop` would say something else entirct for packet-fed seats, and that rule is sound -- but inlining an 18 KB artifact and asking for exhaustive cross-checking gives a thinking model enough to reason itself past its own budget. **Inline the facts; do not inline an entire document and ask for an audit of it.**  *** AND A SIXTH CLASS, MEASURED THE SAME SESSION on the matrix-review panel: THE SEAT\u0027S OWN TRANSPORT DIED MID-ANSWER. *** `agy` returned 293 bytes reading `I have launched the topic cluster analysis script ... Waiting for backgrount a refused connection), it echoed nothing, it emitted a real partial answer rather than an empty response inside vast thinking, and the other seats on the same panel were unaffected (not the shared-Agent-tool outage). **The distinguishing shape: the seat scriminate between them. The honest state of the evidence: burns at 19,395 (per-item audit) and 10,408 (per-item audit); clean answers at 8,583 (single-subject review) and 3,614 (single-subject research). **Size and shape are perfectly correlated across all four data points**, so nothing here separates them. A discriminating test exists and is cheap -- a LARGE single-subject brief, or a SMALL per-item one -- and until someone runs it the cause remains NOT ESTABLISHED. *Recorded because the first stated causn inject bytes into a live DATA-IN transfer and desynchronise the next 32768-byte chunk",
