                            "ev":  "[panel_20260830_095837]  wdcaddtoinbufbound pass 1, READ seat",
                            "outcome":  "REFRAMING-RATIFIED-BUT-A2\u0027s-PREMISE-IS-WRONG",
                            "note":  "*** REFUTED THE BRIEF\u0027S LOAD-BEARING PREMISE BY OPENING THE FIXTURE, AND THE REFUTATION CHANGES WHAT THE ROUND OWES. ***  The brief said any fix keeping foreign bytes out of the DATA-IN stream turns the shipped `re-arm: refills a NON-EMPTY ring too` row RED, so the oracle-correction rule applies unconditionally.  **It does not.**  That row plants its foreign bytes by DIRECT PRIMITIVE CALLS -- five `wdc_addtoinbuf(\u0026e, 0x77)` -- and fires the re-arm with a `MEM_READ`.  **A write-arm fix never touches it.**  Only the re-arm option reds it.  So the protocol is OPTION-CONDITIONAL, and it warned against running it anyway: re-pinning an oracle no code change will redden is expectation churn with no red to show, **which the oracle-correction rule itself calls the laundering signature.**  It then swept every OTHER shipped row for collateral under a write-arm fix and found none: the three `midxfer` rows and both mid-DATAIN write rows assert `stub_frees == 0` with NO occupancy oracle, and their fixtures were already re-pinned so a phase-keying fix does not false-fail.  **A3 confirmed AND UNDERSOLD.**  The severity downgrade is larger than claimed: the source\u0027s `shared ring feeds the CDB-dispatch and drain paths` hedge is ALSO dead, because `wdc_new_command_reset()` flushes at the top of every `wdc_command()`.  Blast radius at HEAD is the guest\u0027s own current transfer plus self-inflicted DRQ ghosting -- **no host-safety, no cross-command reach** -- which ranks it below every row with a host-safety or flood channel, including the two check-after-the-store siblings the brief keeps out of scope.  It required the downgrade be WRITTEN with its carrying rows named, since the row\u0027s `sev` is empty and a reader would otherwise re-derive the old rank from the prose trail.  **A4: ONE STRUCTURALLY DISTINCT OPTION MISSING** -- allowlist-by-DIRECTION (decline unless the device expects host-\u003edevice bytes) rather than blocklisting DATAIN.  That is what real hardware does, and it covers the idle-state and COMPLETED-phase pushes a DATAIN blocklist leaves alive -- today even the `not expecting any` arm announces and then PUSHES ANYWAY.  It also measured that the re-arm option is **a partial fix by construction**: an injection during the LAST chunk has no following re-arm.  **Q2 CONFIRMED, and pinned by a SHIPPED ROW rather than by argument** (`no-push write does not dispatch`: occupancy 12, push-free write, DATAIN, frees 0) -- which it noted is unlike the transferred warrant tnst source."
