                            "outcome":  "WITNESS-BUILT-AND-GREEN-plus-a-FLOOR-FINDING",
                            "note":  "*** THE WITNESS IS BUILT AND IT WORKS -- 20 of 20, both legs, every control green -- AND IT REFUTED TWO OF THE BRIEF\u0027S PREMISES, ONE OF WHICH CHANGES THE ROUND\u0027S DISPOSITION. ***  Badge A disclosed unprompted: it was the opus5 seat on `#494`, so its baseline contains its own fix, same device and file.  **(1) THE SKETCH AS BRIEFED COULD NOT HAVE EXHIBITED THE DEFECT AT ALL.**  I wrote *32 blocks on a CD-ROM* assuming 2048-byte blocks.  In this tree CD-ROM `logical_block_size` is **512** -- the 2048 branch is inside `#if 0` -- so 32 blocks is 16384 bytes, under the 32768 chunk clamp: no second chunk, no re-arm, nothing to measure.  **It needs 128 blocks.**  A seat that had merely followed the brief would have produced a clean run and called the defect absent.  **(2) `ANY FIX THAT KEEPS FOREIGN BYTES OUT TURNS THE SHIPPED ROW RED` IS MEASURED FALSE**, independently confirming what the fable5 adjudication derived by reading the fixture: fixA (write-arm guard) leaves the detector at **128 rows, 0 failures**; only fixB (flush at the re-arm) reds it, at 1.  **So the round is NOT under the oracle-correction rule unless it picks the re-arm option**, and the row is a rare DISCRIMINATOR between the two -- the opposite of the carrier\u0027s *green under every candidate fix, settles nothing* corollary.  *** (3) THE FLOOR FINDING, AND IT GOVERNS THE ROUND: THE SHIPPED 128-ROW DETECTOR DOES NOT OBSERVE THIS DEFECT AT ALL. ***  `base` scores 0 failures WITH THE DEFECT LIVE, so vacuity-floor clause (a) -- fails on the pre-fix build -- is **not satisfiable from existing rows**.  If the round ships the write-arm guard, **the witness must ship AS the detector or it ships below the floor.**  And two one-expression clause-(d) mutants escape the detector entirely (`!= PHASE_CMDOUT` -\u003e `== PHASE_COMPLETED`; `\u0026\u0026 len == 1`), caught only by the witness at 17/20.  **fixA\u0027s zero is a MEANINGFUL zero**, and it proved that rather than asserting it: `mutA1` moves 14 rows on the same arm, so the rows ARE sensitive to a guard there.  That is the negative control for *fixA disturbs nothing*.  **THE WITNESS AND THE DETECTOR ARE COMPLEMENTARY AND NEITHER SUBSUMES THE OTHER** -- mutA1 is caught by the detector and by the witness\u0027s signature control; mutA2/mutA3 only by the witness.  Ship both.  **Two option members missing, and the first is orthogonal to my whole axis:** (e) DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE -- my (a)-(d) are LOCATIONS, refuse-vs-announce is a DISPOSITION and they composeff CMDOUT mid-CDB.  **A LIVE L4 IN PRODUCT CODE:** `#477`\u0027s objection cites the `default:` len-3/8 arm as its example, and `#479` retired that example with `!badlen_this` **in a comment block fifteen lines below it in the same file**.  The warrant wasev_wdc.c` while `build/`, `build-asan/` and `est/` all carried the fix.  A scratch clone taken from it would have measured `#494`-less code in the file under review and `cmp`-ed clean against its own donor.  Propagated and rebuilt with the two-part clearance run; filed as `novpadfourth`.  It also proved SEC moving under its run was behaviourally null rather than asserting it -- compiled both sources with identical flags and found the objects differ in exactly three `push $\u003cline\u003e` constants, each +9, with `.rodata` identical and a negative control showing the comparison CAN fail."
