                            "note":  "*** FOUND FOUR MORE ESCAPES AND A DEFECT IN THE SCORING ITSELF.  Badge A: it authored the pass-1 mutants AND the witness this round ships, and its headline finding is a defect in ITS OWN M3. ***  **E1 `\u0026\u0026 len == 2` -- the MIRROR of its own M3.**  `len == 1` reds 3 rows; `len == 2`, one character away, sweeps clean, because the probe injects with a 2-byte store.  **The round measured the inert member of the family and concluded the family was covered.**  Reproduced independently here at 22/22; repaired by making the second injection a SINGLE byte, which closes the family with one instruction.  **E2 `atapi_cmd_in_progress` -\u003e `atapi_st != NULL` -- and it MEASURED the damage.**  Post-packet push/pop reads `5a,a5` shipped versus `ff,ff` swapped.  `atapi_st` is allocated at first dispatch and never nulled, so after one command the swap refuses every ordinary data-port write for the life of the device.  Correctly ruled NOT a clause-(d) breach by the DEPENDS-ON letter and filed as `wdcatapistswap`.  **E3** reproduced the M5 breach independently.  **E4** exposed that every probe here has only a little-endian leg, so the BE half of every guard in that switch is unpinned by construction -- filed as `wdcprobeendian`.  *** AND THE FINDING IT DID NOT GO LOOKING FOR: THE SCORER CANNOT TELL A KILL FROM A NON-MEASUREMENT. ***  Three of its seven runs were scored `KILLED (20 red)` while measuring nothing -- `words 0 of 46`, pc already at HALT, 0.00 s, **on both legs including the unmutated base that had scored clean minutes earlier**.  Re-run quietly, two ESCAPED.  **Every one carried the completion sentinel**, which proves the probe finished writing and not that it measured.  It named the discriminator correctly and corrected its own first attempt at it: **the BASE LEG, not a threshold** -- a threshold would have rejected M7, whose mutant leg legitimately kills the guest.  Cause: this loop ran a second table concurrently, and it noted the `#489` precedent covers TREE SAFETY, not MEASUREMENT VALIDITY.  It also measured the `#477` coupling to run PROTECTIVE rather than harmful -- removing that test breaks the CDB dispatch by itself, and `#495` makes the failure safer and louder -- so the shipped comment\u0027s direction is backwards (L4).  And it caught that the `else if` skips the `default:` arm, losing `#337`/`#478`\u0027s latched diagnostic for 3- and 8-byte stores, then checked both consumers and found them provably inert in the guard\u0027s own state."
