                    l run and a timing run.  Its framing is the durable part: the deciding variable is not \u0027same file\u0027 (my argument) but \u0027SAME LANDING DATE\u0027, which is conditional on checks the packet had not run.  It also independently corrected the unit error (~73, not ~145) and raised the possibility I had not -- that free-running may not be needed at all, which I then settled by reading: the overrun fatal() is SYNCHRONOUS inside the data-port write handler, so a stepped probe CAN see it and free-running I POSED WAS INCOMPLETE BY THREE MEMBERS, and one of them is aimed\ndirectly at me. ***\n\n  M4  RE-PIN THE WANT TO 0 AND KEEP THE DEAD STIMULUS.  One character; the gate goes green.\n      REJECTED as the oracle-correction rule\u0027s laundering case with ed scored row in the weekly\nbattery is a standing mis-attribution engine, which is what this round exists to prevent.\n\nTWO MUTATIONS OWED, and the second is the anti-fake control:\n  M_relatch  remove the latch guard and flag-set, keep the fatal() and the refusal return.\n             Every refused byte then announces -- expect the count \u003e\u003e 1 against want 1, RED.\n  M_silent   DELETE the producer\u0027s fatal(), keep the guard and the refusal.  The row must\n             read 0, RED.  *** THIS IS WHAT PROVES THE COUNTED 1 COMES FROM THE PRODUCER\u0027S\n             ANNOUNCE and not from a widened regex: the smallest fake is a one-token widening\n             of P_OVERRUN so the datawr line feeds it, and M_silent is the only row-level\n             check that catches it -- a polluted row reads 1 and stays green. ***\n\nFOUR FACTS BEYOND THE BRIEF:\n  1. P4 is disjoint BY DESIGN, not by luck.  #484\u0027s bulk-arm message deliberately names\n     wdc__read() instead of the producer, with an in-source comment saying the shared latch\n     removed the only other way to tell the sites apart.  P_OVERRUN anchors on\n     `wdc_addtoinbuf():`, so the ONLY line in the device that can feed the count is the\n     producer\u0027s own announce.  The regex-to-sh the run and session() reads for a FIXED spin with no completion\n     detection -- so a load-starved spin truncates the transcript BEFORE the announce and the\n     row reads 0.  That is the gate_ab false-FAIL class, sitting in the weekly battery whose\n     rules exist because of it.\n  4. *** MY OWN FRAMING NEEDS A QUALIFIER -- see the L4 correction on the entry below. ***\n\nP3 REMAINS NOT SETTLED and the seat declined to transfer the 171k/s figure, saying it could\nnot locate the number\u0027s provenance.  Neither could I.  That is the right refusal."
