                            "note":  "VERIFIED THE ADJUDICATOR\u0027S COST-HALVING CLAIM RATHER THAN TAKING IT.  `datawr x2` already\ndrives MOV_L_R8_AT_R7 (opcode 0x2782, a FOUR-BYTE store) at WD_DATA, and it is a SHIPPED\nGREEN ROW.  So the len=4 route is proven working on this machine, not hypothesised, and the\nwrite arm\u0027s `case 4` pushes four bytes per store.\n\nARITHMETIC, derived rather than transcribed (WDC_INBUF_SIZE = 262656, capacity 262655):\n\n    byte store   262655 to fill   262695 with margin   ~788087 single-steps\n    half store   131328 to fill   131368 with margin   ~394106 single-steps\n    LONG store    65664 to fill    65704 with margin   ~197114 single-steps\n\nSo the long form is HALF the brief\u0027s cost, for one constant swap and no new mechanism.  The\nseat quoted 65,700 / 197,102; the small difference is the margin choice, not a disagreement.\n\nIT DOES NOT MAKE THE TIMING MEASUREMENT UNNECESSARY -- 197k single-steps is still large, and\nthe load-sensitivity hazard the seat named is unchanged in kind: the announce still fires at\n~99.9% through the run, and session() still reads for a FIXED spin with no completion\ndetection, so a load-starved spin truncates before the announce and the row reads 0.  Halving\nthe run halves the exposure; it does not remove it."
