        "note":  "*** NOT A COSMETIC WARNING -- IT WAS COSTING AN ENTIRE GATE\u0027S COVERAGE, and that was found only by re-running a battery that had been RED AND UNREAD FOR FIVE DAYS. ***  `#472` replaced `len \u003e OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE? OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE : len` with `len \u003e remain? remain : len`, where `len` is `size_t` (parameter) and `remain` is `off_t`.  gcc warns twice at diskimage.c:1382 under the tree\u0027s own CWARNINGS.  **THE CASCADE:** `gate_build` wants ZERO warnings, so it FAILED; it withdraws `$RIG/gxsec-gxemul` at start and republishes only on success; `gate_mips` then `need_exec`s that binary and reported *\u0027SKIP -- missing or non-executable binary\u0027*.  **A whole gate lost, scored as SKIP rather than FAIL** -- byte-identical in shape to what one stale allowlist line cost on 2026-08-23, which is the defect `gatebuildallow` records.  **IT IS NOT A LIVE BUG AND THE ROUND SAYS SO:** `inblock = curofs \u0026 (OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE-1)` gives [0,511], so `remain` is in [1,512] and positive by construction; the conversion is value-preserving at every reachable value.  Both casts are therefore provable, not plausible.  MEASURED, control first: the reconstructed pre-fix line compiles rc=0/44072 b with **2** sign-compare warnings; the shipped source compiles rc=0/44112 b with **0**.  *** MY FIRST VERIFICATION WAS VACUOUS AND ITS OWN CONTROL CAUGHT IT: *** it reported 0 warnings for the PRE-FIX form, which must be 2.  The compile was failing on a missing include and the script read its empty output as a result -- the phantom-absence class, in a script written to prove a fix.  Take 2 reports compile rc and object size BEFORE the warning count and refuses to read the count without them.  EXPOSURE, stated honestly: warnings need a BUILD, builds are too slow for precommit, so warnings are checked only by the weekly battery -- a warning-introducing commit is invisible for up to seven days, and only if someone reads the result.  *** THE ROW NAMED NO COMMIT WHILE THE FIX HAD SHIPPED.  Found 2026-08-30 by reading `src/disk/diskimage.c`: the clamp now reads `lentoread = len \u003e (size_t) remain? remain : (off_t) len;` with a `#491` comment proving both casts safe -- `inblock` is `curofs` masked to [0, OVERLAY_BLOCK_SIZE-1], so `remain` is in [1, 512] and can never be negative. ***  `git log -S` puts it in **18893de**, now recorded.  **This is the same shape a gate caught on `holdmarkermulti` in the same session -- work shipped, row names no commit -- and it did NOT trip here only because the state is `in work` rather than `open`.**  `check_row_states` scopes its shipped-work test to open rows, so an `in work` row can carry shipped code indefinitely without any gate objecting.  *Recorded as an observation about the checker\u0027s scope, not filed as a defect: widening it to `in work` would fire on every round that is genuinely mid-flight, which is what `in work` means.  The honest fix is the habit of filling `commits` at ship time, not a wider gate.*  The row\u0027s own EXPOSURE note stands unchanged and is the important part: warnings need a BUILD, builds are too slow for precommit, so a warning-introducing commit is invisible for up to seven days -- and only then if someone reads the battery result.",
