                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1",
                            "outcome_note":  "REVISE -- the uniform design misdescribes reads, and one shared latch is wrong.  *The proposed uniform \u0027decline + latched announce\u0027 design MISDESCRIBES READS, and a single shared latch would suppress distinct diagnostics.*  Both halves are now confirmed: the read path really does compute its value before the kill (see grok), so describing all twelve arms as one uniform decline is wrong; and a single latch across ten arms means the first wide access anywhere silences the diagnostic for the other nine, which is the shared-latch failure `#498` measured at 23/25 and this session measured again as `M_BITALIAS\u0027.",
