                            "outcome_note":  "Packet-fed. *** P5 WRONG IN BOTH CLAUSES, VERIFIED BY THE MAIN LOOP: the byte arms are NOT reg = idata -- VECBASE \u0026 0xf0, TxICR |= (idata \u0026 0x17) + pending clears, SCCERR = 0, SCC* \u0026 0x1f/0xdf -- and reassert_interrupts is in SIX arms, not two. *** And it derived the cleanest justification of the split: the read path uses raw data in address order (width-correct by construction); every write arm uses idata, which means the addressed byte only at len==1. Reads: delete the discard. Writes: cannot be fixed without per-arm semantics. Decline follows. Two more unnamed members: first-byte-only accept; FAULT\u0027s feasibility not in the packet (what does the caller do with return 0?). The witness cannot protect the fix: no byte-write row, no value rows.",
                            "note":  "Packet-fed. *** P5 WRONG IN BOTH CLAUSES, VERIFIED BY THE MAIN LOOP: the byte arms are NOT reg = idata -- VECBASE \u0026 0xf0, TxICR |= (idata \u0026 0x17) + pending clears, SCCERR = 0, SCC* \u0026 0x1f/0xdf -- and reassert_interrupts is in SIX arms, not two. *** And it derived the cleanest justification of the split: the read path uses raw data in address order (width-correct by construction); every write arm uses idata, which means the addressed byte only at len==1. Reads: delete the discard. Writes: cannot be fixed without per-arm semantics. Decline follows. Two more unnamed members: first-byte-only accept; FAULT\u0027s feasibility not in the packet (what does the caller do with return 0?). The witness cannot protect the fix: no byte-write row, no value rows."
