                            "note":  "PASS 7, FILE-READING (walked all twelve write bodies in the fork; line numbers match).  VERDICT NO-GO on closing: the three pass-6 cells are closed, the operand-space sentence is not -- the IPL write body reads a function-static `w\u0027 (`if (!w) { fatal; w = 1; }\u0027) and no row holds it SET at a wide write, so `\u0026\u0026 !w\u0027 on the IPL width guard is equivalent on all 159 rows; the distinguishing session is one st.b to IPL then a wide write, DECL 1 vs 0.  Same rule as pass 5\u0027s `warned\u0027 and pass 6\u0027s pending: L2, one row.  Also: PRETABLE_pass6b Section 13 lists SCCTX\u0027s landed lane as 0x44 -- SCCTX is `\u0026 0x1f\u0027 like SCCICR, so 0x04 (kill holds; grouped with SCCRX by mistake); premise 7 \u0027written ONLY by pcc_timer_tick\u0027 is FALSE (the TxICR body clears and decrements; the tick is the only producer of \u003e 0); the MASK arm comment claims a `static int w\u0027 the MASK body does not have (copy-paste from IPL, earlier pass, wrong record); the CHANGELOG\u0027s part-6b RED line is truncated at `rb8\u0027 (a `cut -c1-200\u0027 in the fill); rd(8.0) is a wall-clock drain, not a prompt wait -- under load `print r4\u0027 is sent to a running guest, `pend* arm\u0027 prints `died\u0027 falsely and decl/rb fail for a reason other than the one under test -\u003e it should say FAILED FOR SOME OTHER REASON.  Verified right: the 0x31 liveness+signature claim (bb0 0x34 no-delay-slot, d16 -1 = previous instruction; INT only via reassert), the landed-lane tables at both widths, the transfer of the four part-6 scores, the L2 ruling on the pending qualifier (agrees), the out-of-closure claims for reg[IPL] and cur_int_vec[].  Denominator stated.  A READING with source verification."
