                            "ev":  "_scratchpad/panel_20260904_033322",
                            "note":  "PASS 7, FILE-READING (pointer-fed; 440 KB stream, answer at the tail).  VERDICT NO-GO.  (1) TxCTL\u0027s body is an RMW that PRESERVES the upper-nibble overflow state (PCC2_TCTL_OVF, set only by pcc_timer_tick on a count overflow); every TxCTL preset has that nibble zero, so `\u0026\u0026 !(d-\u003epcctwo_reg[relative_addr] \u0026 PCC2_TCTL_OVF)\u0027 at the TxCTL guard is predicted 159/159 -- the byte was counted covered because its LOW bits are non-initial, inconsistent with enumerating TxICR\u0027s INT bit separately.  (2) No rb4/rb8 rows at T1CTL/T1ICR: `if (len \u003c 4 || relative_addr == PCCTWO_T2CTL) break;\u0027 announces and lands len 4/8 at T1CTL while every T1 halfword row and every T2 wide row stays green -- the T1/T2 split the contract recognised at len 2 owes its width cross-product.  (3) rd(8.0) drains the pty for eight seconds without recognising a prompt; under starvation later commands reach a running guest and the final waitpid() can HANG the detector; `pend* arm\u0027 prints `died\u0027 while the child is alive -- distinguish timeout/no-breakpoint, no-r4, died:\u003cstatus\u003e, with boundedu0027nine of nine answered\u0027 is impossible with agy not fired (eight answering of nine); the CHANGELOG part-6b RED line truncated; PRETABLE_pass6b\u0027s mtime equals the part6/driver.log COPY\u0027s second, so it witnesses precedence over 6b, not strict order after 6; the transfer of the four scores is defensible; the landed-lane tables agree with grok\u0027s (SCCTX 0x04 at len 8).  Three of its findings are one class: device state that presets cannot reach (OVF nibble, static w) -- the enumeration must be by body-read LVALUE with its full bit-domain."
