                            "note":  "PASS 11, self-declared claude-fable-5-1 (badge s), the RULE-QUESTION seat asked to be harder on ITS OWN pass-10 rule.  Liveness token + the CHECKPOINT gate line returned; tree verified (b78bb0f + working set, probe md5 6676c58d, constants against mvme_pcctworeg.h and dev_pcc2.c:515-543).  VERDICT: CLOSE provided clause (d) is bounded per its H1 answer, plus one L4; under the rule read LITERALLY, DO NOT CLOSE.  Q1: accepted #9 is WRONG (0x08 \u0026 0x17 == 0 -- ICLR is excluded from the store mask, which is exactly WHY bit 3 is dead; the correction reversed the mechanism: \u0027a correction is not safer than the thing it corrects\u0027); the other fifteen defensible, but #7\u0027s warrant (\u0027row IEN because body-tested\u0027) is the seed of the H1 inconsistency -- IEN is over-coverage, not floor; R1-R3 right relative to the adopted rule, and R3/minimax and the pass-9 dissent \u0027correctly sensed the exponentiality H1 must fix\u0027.  H1: its own rule AS WRITTEN demands all 128 cells and is #392-prone (2^k in the if-count, compounding across twelve arms); the FLOOR it SHOULD demand = {dominating predicates} x {device-STATE lvalues the fix\u0027s own repair path reads that are JOINTLY REACHABLE through its own data flow} = {label} x {p1} x {p2} = 8 cells, all rowed (over-covered by the 16); the bits of the single idata being written are single-operand MARGINALS, not floor; the ICLR/INT/0xe0 joints are clause-(e) coverage debt subject to the one ask-again; \u0027a filter may reject or discharge a cell but demand a new row only for a floor cell, so it cannot grow unbounded\u0027.  Opus\u0027s incremental value-class form reaches the same result at this arm but is CIRCULAR as a floor (defined by what is already rowed, so it cannot fail).  Q3: the nine rows sound; landed values 0x00/0x13/0x33/0x20 never the preset; \u0027decl counts of 4\u0027 in the brief was stale (rows want 1; the tree already corrected it).  Q4: all six measurements re-derived; the M_PENDBOTH misprediction correctly recorded; confirms pendboth rb1i = 0x33 independently.  Q5: the smallest escape is the 2-axis `\u0026\u0026 !((idata \u0026 ICLR) \u0026\u0026 p2)\u0027 -- reachable via put h T2ICR 0x0008 while timer 2 pends; disclosed by the contract, clause (e), above floor.  ADJUDICATED: the bounded floor ADOPTED (the author of the rule ruling against its letter); the ICLR/0xe0 x pending cells are taken as L1 CONSTRUCTION with a MEASURED warrant (Opus\u0027s M_ICLR) in grok\u0027s generating-set form -- a set/clear pair per idata axis at every rowed pending cell -- so every single-axis extra conjunct reds; multi-axis idata joints at pending cells stay disclosed; INT-clear x pending\u003e0 disclosed as unreachable with the derivation (grok)."
