                            "note":  "PASS 11, FILE-READING + MEASURING (own clone /tmp/gxopus_p11, cmp-clean, baseline rebuilt, mutant gcc-syntax-checked before the table, restored from SEC + rebuilt + cmp-clean, sentinel cleared; project trees never written).  VERDICT DO NOT CLOSE.  MEASURED: BASE 203/203 (md5 6676c58d); `M_ICLR\u0027 = `\u0026\u0026 !(p2 \u0026\u0026 (idata \u0026 ICLR))\u0027 203/203 TOTAL ESCAPE (predicted 16:56 before its build) with a POSITIVE CONTROL proving the write LANDS (mutant CONTROL_RB=0x13 DECL=0 vs baseline 0x31 DECL=1 -- entering the cell corrupts the register and silently consumes a pending timer interrupt); BASE2 203/203 on the post-edit instrument 12c7a97b, closing a ONE-INSTRUMENT STRADDLE it reports on itself (its runner re-copied the live probe between BASE and M_ICLR while the main loop applied docstring-only L4s at 17:12 -- 7 text lines, 203 identical (name, want) pairs).  Q1: #9 wrong (0x17 \u0026 0x08 == 0; ~0x17 = 0xE8 preserves bit 3; writer census of reg[0x1a/0x1b]: :516/:517 mask, :537 \u0026= ~INT, :279/:282 |= INT, the memcpy spans at most 0x18 -- bit 3 has NO writer); F2 #2\u0027s \u0027int is not finite\u0027 (credit codex/glm); R1-R3 right; its OWN pass-9 dissent was wrong (\u0027a rule that lets the author decide which mutants are edits anyone writes is not a rule\u0027); #12 holds; and it WITHDRAWS half its own pass-10 bound (\u0027demand INCREMENTAL\u0027 has no stopping rule -- the dissent in a hat) while pressing the other half: \u0027dispatch axes as full axes\u0027 demands the T1/T2 axis at TxCTL where relative_addr is an RMW INDEX no `if\u0027 tests, which the body-tested form misses.  H1: YES -- the adopted rule\u0027s text has no exemption; the \u0027DOES, not lands\u0027 warrant refutes itself (no body-tested partition governs landing -- p1, p2, IEN included); the escape is a TWO-way conjunction hiding inside a count-only disclosure, on the interrupt-ACKNOWLEDGE path -- the most-travelled state the register has; and it is L2 BY THE ROUND\u0027S OWN PASS-3 SENTENCE (probe:1062-1064: \u0027a disclosure cannot discharge a floor clause, or every breach becomes a sentence\u0027) -- inside the closure on every candidate bound.  ITS BOUND: axes = lvalues the body\u0027s code makes DECISIVE (tested in an `if\u0027 OR used as an index/selector); demand = a COVERING ARRAY OF STRENGTH t, t = the longest conjunction the body itself writes (4 here), cost O(2^t log k) not 2^k; DISCLOSE BY STRENGTH (\u0027kills every conjunction of at most t of the N axes\u0027 -- falsifiable, would have made this escape unwritable); t and the axis list read off the diff ONCE, no pass may raise t.  \u0027The round has already designed the repair and it is sound\u0027 -- 0x0018 (landed 0x10), 0x0020 (0x20 armed / 0x00 idle + the HUH? print as a second channel), twelve readbacks and three huh rows; its own \u0027six to nine writes\u0027 was an undercount.  Records: \u0027about thirty more wide writes\u0027 has no deriver and is wrong (one write per cell: 112 syntactic, at most 96 reachable, 16 rowed, 80 open -- the (same-timer count \u003e 0, INT clear) cells unreachable at a guard, caveat the SIGALRM/DEVICE_TICK window = filed pcc2iclrdec); the (T1, 0, 0, IEN clear) cell is credited to `latch all\u0027 which iterates BLOCKS12 at 0x1a and NEVER writes T1ICR -- the cell is held by `op t1icr dcl\u0027 (0x0303): the named channel is structurally blind to the cell (L4, owed); cval()\u0027s value branch emits a bare `died\u0027 on a LIVE guest with a short transcript (one-line fix, owed); the brief\u0027s clause (d) was labelled VERBATIM but superseded on disk mid-pass (process defect: a packet should carry the carrier\u0027s revision).  Derived, NOT measured, for pass 12: at TxCTL the rule enumerates {COVF} x {idata \u0026 ~7} with no label axis and two of four cells unheld -- `\u0026\u0026 !((idata \u0026 COVF) \u0026\u0026 !(idata \u0026 ~7))\u0027 predicted to sweep 203, reachable by st.h 0x0004 a