ted to L2; (6) pcc2huhflood\u0027s \u0027acc all trips SCCICR/SCCTX\u0027 is false (0x10 \u0026 ~0x1f == 0) -- CONFIRMED; the main loop\u0027s correction said \u0027it trips VECBASE\u0027, ALSO false (0x10 \u0026 ~0xf0 == 0; it trips TxCTL and PSCALEADJ only) -- caught by the Opus pass-13 seat, filing corrected twice; (7) \u0027a debugger-visible read clears SCCRX INT\u0027 -- pcc2 is DM_DEFAULT so `dump\u0027 bypasses it; a GUEST read does -- CONFIRMED, addendum corrected.  Queue: pcc2defaultkill promoted to HIGH (an unimplemented offset kills the host; OpenBSD\u0027s if_ie.c writes 0x2a); pscaleflood folded into huhflood; widecompose file-and-leave.  Rule: adopts the Opus strength-t bound (DISSENT from the adjudicator, recorded).  Its part-12 reading was made before the part-12 dir was preserved (it read the live driver log mid-run: two of three results seen)."
