    {
        "id":  "lunaabsentcpu",
        "title":  "lunaabsentcpu  dev_luna88k.c reassert_interrupts() calls the NULL interrupt callback of an UNCONFIGURED cpu slot: on the default one-cpu luna-88k two ordinary guest word stores (INT_ST_MASK1 then SOFT_INT1)onnect guards are 0.7.0 code); #438 removed the exit(1) on low bits in the SAME arm; its probe\u0027s D4 row stores 0x84000100 to MASK1 (bits 31, 26, 8 -- bit 26 SET, slot 1 ARMED for the rest of that session) and could not see this only because a cold debachine-\u003encpus\u0027); (b) declining stores to absent slots is REJECTED for this round (an unsourced board-model claim, changes guest-visible readback, reddens two shipped es438 rows D4/E2) and FILED as the question row lunaabsentmaskdecl; (c) a no-op connection fabricates plumbing with no in-tree idiom; (e) a NULL check guards the symptom.  Detector: W1 kill row + the connected-slot control + a `-n 2\u0027 ACCEPT row whose channel is cpu 1 ASSERTING (irq_asserted / vector entry), not survival; PRETABLEtra (codex, max effort, read-only) predicted it from the source (\u0027interrupt delivery can still reach an unconnected CPU callback\u0027); the main loop built and ran the witness the same evening; Fable 5.1 adjudication of batch 7 in flight.  The fix round runs the full nine-seat panel.",
        "state_note":  "\n\n=== MAIN-LOOP ROUND RECORDS, 2026-09-06 -- moved out of the per-seat `entries\u0027 column ===\nThese are the round\u0027s OWN records -- table results, repair descriptions, stage summaries an\nan established convention (every other entry in the ledger uses a declared seat).  The seat column is the\nper-seat record that check_boilerplate, check_seats_read and the scorecard all read, so a round note living\nthere is a round note wearing a seat\u0027s clothes -- the stamped-summary shape one level up.  Moved here verbatim;\nthe same material is in the CHANGELOG round block.\n\n  [2026-09-06 / review] PASS-2 REPAIR (one diff): fix capture moved below the `ncpus \u003e 4` exit; probe v3 adds sessions B2 (sio5 deliver), C2 (both deliver) and E (-n 4: four cpus / cpu3 deliver / others idle); docstring corrections; mutants M_MASK30, M_SWONLY, M_IRQACTIVE0, M_AND1, M_MIN2 added to the eleven; PRETABLE2 written before table 2 (corrections to go to a separate file).  Table 1 (killtable/, v2, 22 rows): BASE 22/22 PASS; M_REVERT/M_OFFBY1/M_LATCH 15/17, M_NULLA/M_GUARDASSERT 16/17, M_NOASSIGN 17/19, M_HARD1/M_SKIP1 19/20, M_NULLAB 22/22 (equivalent), M_NOREASSERT 22/22 (debt), M_CALLGUARD 16/18 -- the pass-1 F4 alternative measured NOT a fix (sio5, siofirst HALT: the SIO line reaches the walk through the device-line callers).  HEAD 15/17 PRE_FIX_SYMPTOM (soft1, siofirst; the denominator drops from 22 when the host dies mid-session).\n\n  [2026-09-05 / assess] WITNESS built before any edit (rung 3, unmodified -e luna-88k): two supervisor stores (INT_ST_MASK1 \u003c- 0xfc000000, SOFT_INT1 \u003c- 1) on the default one-cpu machine end the emulator with SIGSEGV -- witness_head_20260905_2130.out.  Filed from retrospective batch 7 (Fable adjudication of the m8820x rounds) after the #438 probe missed it: that probe stored 0x84000100 (bit 26 SET) but never stored SOFT_INT1, so nothing was pending when the walk ran.\n\n  [2026-09-06 / review] PASS-3 REPAIR (probe v4 -\u003e v5, 34 rows, frozen v5 md5 3fd0198f; fix v2b unchanged): v4 added sessions B3 (redeliver, reenter, noreenter) and C3 (noreenter1) for the deassert side (deepseek, minimax) and pended slots 2 AND 3 in E (grok, kimi: M_SKIP2); v5 (kimi, landed after v4 was cut) pends ALL FOUR slots in E (cpu0/cpu1 deliver4, others-idle removed) and adds C4 (sio5 deliver1: a device line to slot 1).  TABLE 3 (killtable3/) and TABLE 4 (killtable4/, PRETABLE4 written 11:00 before the 11:31 start, untouched): 22 mutants, BASE 34/34 before and after, clone cmp-clean; every mutant killed except M_NULLAB 34/34 -- PREDICTED EQUIVALENT (a both-sided NULL guard is the same predicate as the bound on every reachable configuration; DEVINIT connects exactly slots 0..ncpus-1 and the ncpus \u003e 4 exit bounds ncpus), recorded as an alternative fix with its warrant, not a breach.  M_IRQACTIVEP1 32/34 (cpu2/cpu3 deliver: the parity alias), M_NOREASSERT 31/33 (killed by the noreenter rows; the v2/v3 disclosure withdrawn), M_CALLGUARD 28/30 (pass 2 had predicted it equivalent; it is not).  HEAD 83df95c with v5: 27/29 PRE_FIX_SYMPTOM (soft1, siofirst).  PRETABLE4\u0027s one mis-prediction was in the safe direction (it said M_NOREASSERT would stay green on the NEW rows; it stays killed by the v4 rows).  Pass 4 (closing) fired to the scriptable seats at ~12:28 (brief_lunaabs_p4.md); Opus 5 / Fable 5 owed when the wall lifts.\n\n  [2026-09-06 / review] PASS-4 REPAIR, graded L2 (a clause-(d) floor breach: an operand swap drawn from a field the guarded body READS, on the predicate dominating the walk\u0027s body) -- repaired IN-ROUND, not filed.  Because passes 3 and 4 both found breaches of the {slot} x {per-cpu array} alias class, the repair closes the CLASS in one diff rather than the cell: probe v6 (md5 3be01e9d) RESTORES v4\u0027s session E beside v5\u0027s all-four E as session E2 (slots 2 and 3 pending, 0 and 1 idle; rows cpu3 deliver23, cpu2 deliver23, others idle23 -- 37 rows), in which every per-cpu array the walk touches has a disagreeing al**  That clause said an EMPTY interrupt name installs non-NULL `no_interrupt_assert\u0027 / `no_interrupt_deassert\u0027 stubs, so `has a callback\u0027 and `slot \u003c ncpus\u0027 differ in MECHANISM.  Read `src/core/interrupt.c\u0027 (anchor `if (name[0] ==\u0027 the empty-string test): the arm assigns the stubs and **DOES NOT RETURN** -- the handler scan runs immediately after it, and an unregistered name falls through to `printf(... failed)\u0027 and `abort()`.  So the stub path is DEAD unless the empt M_NULLAB equivalence is UNAFFECTED and the fix is not reopened; only the expiry sentence is corrected.  (2) **THE PASS-5 PACKET NAMES THE WRONG RED ROWS FOR M_IRQACTIVEP1.**  Its table says `cpu2 deliver23, cpu3 deliver23\u0027 (session E2).  killtable5/d exists for the READ aliases and correctly does not red here.  A transcription error in a packet that had the log open beside it.  **WHAT THE TWO SEATS RULED ON THE ROUND\u0027S ONE QUESTION: the closure bound HOLDS.**  grok: `function of cpu alone\u0027 is the right bound for THIS class, with the derivation -- the one-cpu session forces f(0)=0, session C forces f(1)=1, session E2 forces f({2,3}) inside {2,3}, so every single-token map except the identity dies; cells outside f(cpu) are body-field indices (` clean-sweep sits in the remainder.  **ONE REAL PROBE DEFECT, ship-time rather than a new pass (grok): session E2 never sets cpu 0\u0027s VBR/PSR, though session E does.**  So `others idle23\u0027 can see a steal onto cpu 1 (M_AND1 reads BADREGS with pcs[1] at the vector) and CANNOT see one onto cpu 0 -- a CHANNEL filter on an existing row, not a new cell.  Fix: copy E\u0027s two sends.  Both seats also note the product-comment L4 is still present in killtable5/baseline_dev_luna88k.c -- correct, and it stays: that file is the frozen record of what the table ran.  The SHIPPING script (fix_lunaabs.py) was corrected before either answer landed.\n\n=== TABLE 6, 2026-09-06 ===\nTABLE 6 (regress/artifacts/lunaabsentcpu/killtable6_codexpred/), run against codex\u0027s two predictions on the shipped 37-row instrument.  BASE 37/37 opening and closing; scratch clone clean against SEC; no sentinel left; frozen probe md5 7170ae7a.  **M_LOWBIT `cpu \u003c (d-\u003encpus \u0026 -d-\u003encpus)`: 37/37, TOTAL ESCAPE.  M_SOFTAND1 `software_interrupt_status[cpu]\u00261`: 37/37, TOTAL ESCAPE.**  *** BOTH ARE MEMBERS OF FAMILIES THIS PROBE HAD ALREADY DISCLOSED, WHICH IS CLAUSE (e) WORKING RATHER THAN A FLOOR BREACH. ***  M_SOFTAND1 is the `== 1` cell opus5 disclosed on pass 4 ( ran).  Closure filed as lunancpus3.\n\n\n*** CLOSED 2026-09-07 AS A RECORDS CORRECTION.  THE FIX SHIPPED IN `79cd12e` ON 2026-09-06 AND THE\nROW WAS NEVER UPDATED. ***\n\n`dev_luna88k.c` carries the repair BY NAME: *\"#503 (lunaabsentcpu): bound `reassert_interrupts()` to\nthe slots connected above.  It walked all MAX_CPUS and called the NULL interrupt_assert of an\nunpopulated slot ... measured, `regress/luna_absentcpu_probe.py`.\"*  The loop bound changed from\n`cpu \u003c MAX_CPUS` to `cpu \u003c d-\u003encpus`, the `ncpus` snapshot field was added with its own comment, and\nthe 48 kB probe was committed in the same commit.  Kill tables ran; two total escapes were measured\nand both disposed under clause (e) as members of families the probe had already disclosed; the\nresidual is filed as `lunancpus3`.\n\n**So the work was complete and only the row was wrong** -- state `open`, `commits` empty, severity\nHIGH.  It inflated the open-HIGH count and would have misled anyone picking the next round: I\nreported `check_row_states` verifies that no open row\nNAMES a committed detector, and this row named nothing; `check_bugfile_sync` and `check_witness` both\npass on it.  *A row can be complete in the tree and open in the ledger with every gate green.*",
