note: *** THE SAME CLASS #337 FIXED IN dev_wdc.c AND #497 FIXED IN dev_sgi_re.c, AT TWICE THE SITE COUNT, IN A FILE NOBODY HAS EXAMINED. ***  A guest choosing an access width is not an emulator error; here every register in the block insists on a byte and ends the host process otherwise.  **REACHABILITY IS STRONGER THAN `sgidewidth`'s, and this time I checked the domain before saying so.**  `sgidewidth`'s exotic widths turned out unreachable because the MIPS core raises ADEL/ADES first.  **No such filter helps here: the killing widths are 2, 4 and 8 -- all ORDINARY, all naturally alignable.**  A plain aligned 4-byte read of `PCCTWO_GENCTL` needs no misalignment, no truncation and no unusual instruction.  *** HOW IT WAS FOUND, because the method transfers and the finding is a symptom of it: *** a ...[middle omitted]... 2,0x0 ; [0xfff4201c] = 0x00000042` followed by the SCCERR message, and both controls (`put b` -> 0 device messages, `put w` -> 1) are independent of the exit status.  *So the witness stays a real rung-3 reproduction; what was broken was the death OBSERVABLE, not the reachability.*  *** IT BREAKS A RULE I WROTE INTO THE CHECKPOINT THE SAME MORNING -- *never pipe a gate through a filter when you need its exit status* -- which is this project's own finding that knowing a rule and having it fire on the right object are different problems.  I wrote the rule about GATES and then piped a WITNESS. ***
