note: *** EIGHT DATED EXEMPTIONS EXPIRE ON ONE DAY, AND THE CHECKER HARD-FAILS.  MEASURED, NOT REASONED. ***      python tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py --today 2026-09-19   ->  PROBEWIRING_PASS  (46/54 gated, 8 dated-exempt)
    python tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py --today 2026-09-21   ->  PROBEWIRING_FAIL  8 problem(s)
So **every commit after 2026-09-20 is blocked** until all eight are wired or the dates are moved.  The checker is right to do this -- a dated exemption that never comes due is not an exemption -- but eight coming due together is a scheduling hazard rather than a deadline.  *** AND THE POPULATION IS TWICE WHAT THE REGRESS REVIEW NAMED. ***  That review found *'FOUR wdc probes share the single-leg-mode debt and the same 2026-09-20 expiry'* and recommended ONE design ro ...[middle omitted]... ollows from that: (a) and (b) are mechanical, (c) needs one decision, (d) needs a measurement.  Three of the four can ship before the wdc design round even starts.*  *** `8404520` NAMED: that commit shipped this row's FIRST piece of code -- the `PIT8253_LATCH_DONE` sentinel -- and the attribution check refused the NEXT commit until the row said so.  Third time today this rule has fired (after `census` and `wdcatapistswap`), and every one was a real gap rather than a nuisance. ***  The row stays OPEN: one of eight probes is unblocked, seven remain, and the cliff is unmoved until they are wired.
