note:   *** CITATIONS RE-DERIVED 2026-08-31 AND BOTH LOOK STALE. ***  This row cites `gate_hygiene.sh:97-98`; today those are comment lines about harness code being left in scope, not about prompt detection.  The subject -- promptless pty probes -- is discussed at the comment *"TEN pty-forking promptless probes sat"*, and note the COUNT there is TEN while this row's title says SIX.  **Two possibilities and I did not resolve them: either the row is scoped to a subset, or one of the two counts has drifted.**  Recorded as an open question rather than guessed, because picking one would be exactly the kind of confident reconciliation the wrong-tree and stale-citation rules both warn against.  **DURABLE ANCHOR: `grep -n 'promptless probes' regress/gate_hygiene.sh`.**  *ANCHOR CAVEAT, stated rather tha ...[middle omitted]... osed in the gate comment rather than absorbed.*  *TITLE CORRECTED 2026-08-31.  It read "six pty probes have NO prompt detection at all"; re-derived with the gate's OWN computation the live count is **15** -- 11 grandfathered plus 4 that had arrived since the pin was set.  The old figure named neither its unit nor its method and could not be checked, which is exactly the class the counts rule exists for.  The gate comment's competing "TEN" was never the same population: it counts promptless probes under `artifacts/`, which the denominator deliberately excludes, and that population is 20 today.*

