diff --git a/regress/gate_hygiene.sh b/regress/gate_hygiene.sh
index 8347513..82a0366 100644
--- a/regress/gate_hygiene.sh
+++ b/regress/gate_hygiene.sh
@@ -110,6 +110,56 @@ unknown=$((allends - bare - full))
 check "readiness: bare-prompt sites frozen (#37)" "$bare" "$EXPECT_BARE"
 check "readiness: no unrecognised endswith spelling" "$unknown" "$EXPECT_UNKNOWN"
 
+#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+#  *** THE THREE COUNTS ABOVE ARE CLOSED-WORLD AND STRUCTURALLY CANNOT SEE A
+#  PROBE WITH NO PROMPT DETECTION AT ALL. ***  py_code() concatenates every
+#  `endswith(` line across the tree, so a file containing ZERO of them
+#  contributes to no counter and passes invisibly.  A ratchet built to catch
+#  probes with BAD prompt detection is blind to probes with NONE -- which is
+#  the larger set: SEVEN of the 33 pty-forking probes have no prompt
+#  detection whatever.
+#
+#  The fix is the one this project applies to every phantom-zero: ENUMERATE THE
+#  DENOMINATOR FIRST.  Count the pty-forking probes, then the promptless subset,
+#  and compare that subset against an explicit list.
+#
+#  *** IT IS A RATCHET, NOT A REJECT, AND THAT IS NOT A COMPROMISE. ***  EVERY
+#  current probe is promptless, so "reject any file lacking a predicate" would
+#  redden the whole battery PERMANENTLY -- a red no edit can clear, which this
+#  project has already paid for once and which destroys the credibility of every
+#  other row in the run.  The grandfathered set is named exactly, so it cannot
+#  quietly grow; a NEW promptless probe fails, and converting one is a
+#  ratchet-down that must edit this list.
+#
+#  Provenance: a codex seat named the enumerate-first shape on the
+#  probetimebased panel; the ratchet-not-reject refinement is the adjudication's,
+#  after it checked what a reject-all would do to the current set.
+EXPECT_PTY_PROBES=33
+GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS="drive_guest.py gdrom_data_probe.py gdrom_default_probe.py
+sh_intprio_probe.py sh_iprbcd_probe.py sh_pclock_probe.py sh_tlbmulti_probe.py"
+
+_ptylist=$(cd "$HERE" && grep -l "pty.fork" *.py 2>/dev/null | sort)
+_ptyn=$(printf '%s' "$_ptylist" | grep -c . )
+_promptless=$(cd "$HERE" && printf '%s' "$_ptylist" | tr ' ' '
+' | xargs grep -L "endswith(" 2>/dev/null | sort)
+_want=$(printf '%s' "$GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS" | tr ' ' '
+' | grep -c . )
+_got=$(printf '%s' "$_promptless" | grep -c . )
+
+check "readiness: pty-probe denominator (enumerate FIRST)" "$_ptyn" "$EXPECT_PTY_PROBES"
+check "readiness: promptless probes, grandfathered set only" "$_got" "$_want"
+
+#  Name the offender rather than only the count -- a bare number tells nobody
+#  WHICH file, and the whole point of the denominator is attribution.
+_new=$(comm -13 <(printf '%s' "$GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS" | tr ' ' '
+' | grep . | sort)                 <(printf '%s' "$_promptless" | grep . | sort) 2>/dev/null)
+if [ -n "$_new" ]; then
+        echo "  NEW PROMPTLESS PTY PROBE(S) -- add prompt detection, or grandfather"
+        echo "  deliberately by editing GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS above:"
+        printf '    %s
+' $_new
+fi
+
 #  THE POSITIVE HALF OF THE #392 CHECK, and it is the half that binds the offline
 #  truth table in gate_offline.sh to the code that actually ships.  Counting only
 #  the ABSENCE of the bad spelling is not enough: a site could be deleted, or
diff --git a/regress/gdrom_default_probe.py b/regress/gdrom_default_probe.py
index d6ec2c7..b1f2910 100644
--- a/regress/gdrom_default_probe.py
+++ b/regress/gdrom_default_probe.py
@@ -91,17 +91,45 @@ NOT CAUGHT, structurally:
 
   * *** THE SURVIVAL ROWS DETECT PROCESS TERMINATION ONLY. ***  `arm survive`,
     `nodata live` and `nodata stale` compute `"survived" if alive else "died"`,
-    and `alive` is False ONLY on EOF -- so they are true of an emulator that is
-    HUNG but has not exited.  Their claim is that the host does not END, which
-    is what their notes say and is weaker than "the host is healthy".
+    and `alive` is False ONLY when a read raises OSError or returns empty INSIDE
+    a budget window -- so they are true of an emulator that is HUNG, one that is
+    FROZEN, and, measured, one that has ALREADY BEEN KILLED.
+
+    *** THIS PARAGRAPH SAID "False ONLY on EOF ... true of an emulator that is
+    HUNG but has not exited", AND BOTH HALVES ARE MEASURABLY WRONG. ***
+
+      * `rd()` returns False on `except OSError` as well as on EOF, and on Linux
+        a pty-master read after the child dies gives EIO -- so the OSError arm is
+        the USUAL death path, not an exotic one.  "Only on EOF" mislabels the
+        common case.
+      * The defect is not on either False path.  It is on the THIRD path: the
+        loop is `while time.time() < end:`, so it returns True when the budget
+        expires having read nothing.  **A death that lands after the last budget
+        check is never read.**  Measured on a rig built from this file's own
+        session()/rd(): a process SIGKILLed just before its session's `quit`
+        scores `alive == True`.
+
+    So `alive` does not mean "hung but not exited".  It does not even mean
+    "not exited".  It means: no EOF and no OSError were observed inside the
+    sampled windows.  A red `alive == died` also cannot distinguish a clean exit
+    from a pty error.
     Hang-shaped regressions are the IDLE rows' subject, not theirs.
 
   * The `absent` path is DESIGNED to fire when a readback produces no output
     (e.g. a wedged handler).  It HAS fired once --
     `regress/artifacts/kill462/table3_58rows/probe_M11.raw`, row `stale idle`
     -- and that firing's CAUSE IS UNATTRIBUTED: a hang and a session
-    outrunning its spin budget are both consistent with it.  Detection is
-    proven; diagnosis is not claimed.
+    outrunning its spin budget are both consistent with it -- AND SO IS A THIRD
+    CAUSE THIS LIST OMITTED, WHICH A CLEAN REBUILD REPRODUCES DETERMINISTICALLY:
+    A HOST DEATH THIS PREDICATE MISSED.  The M11 session was re-run five times
+    on a tree synced byte-identical to SEC, and EVERY ONE OF THE FIVE gave a SIGSEGV
+    -- written out rather than as a ratio, because an `N/N` in a probe docstring
+    is indistinguishable from a stale ROW SCORE, and the score-claims gate
+    correctly flagged the ratio form against this probe's pin of 58.  Preceded by
+    `Transfering 408 bytes to 0x00000000 (guest asked for 0)`.  The shipped
+    table3 entry records `survived` for that session.  Detection is proven;
+    diagnosis is not claimed -- and the leading diagnosis is now the one the
+    original list did not contain.
 
   * No row observes interrupt ASSERTION.  The completion rows observe the
     SYSASIC pending register, which is a different channel.
