Two distinctions matter for closure: the landisk driver can attach the optional disk, but I found no gate assertion that would fail if that attachment disappeared. GD-ROM warn-bit capacity is protected by a compiler assertion, while DMA write-width behavior remains deliberately unchanged pending an oracle. The wiring deadline now covers six exemptions; PIT and SH4 BSC have been wired.
